hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","1803 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Samura about the narration of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gives one of you good, let him begin with himself and his family."
"1802","1804 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, both said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the evening of Friday when Maiz al-Aslami was stoned, saying: A band of Muslims will conquer the White House. I said: Kisra (Chosroes)? He said: Kisra."
"1803","1805 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will extract the treasure of the White One - Kisra and the family of Kisra."
"1804","1806 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, both said: Hatim ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am the forerunner (al-farat) at the Pond."
"1805","1807 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Muhajir, from Amir, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Pond."
"1806","1808 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The religion will remain standing until there are twelve caliphs from Quraysh; then liars will emerge before the Hour."
"1807","1809 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from al-Muhajir, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The religion will remain standing until the Hour comes, or there are twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."
"1808","Chapter: Tamim ibn Tarafa al-Tai from Jabir ibn Samura. 1810 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim al-Tai, from Jabir ibn Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not line up behind me as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: And how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row."
"1809","1811 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us and said: Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row."
"1810","1812 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Tamim ibn Tarafa al-Tai, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row."
"1811","1813 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not line up as the angels who are with their Lord line up? They said: And how do the angels who are with their Lord line up? He said: They establish the first rows and stand pressed together in the row."
"1812","1814 - Ubaydullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid al-Sulami al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from Sulayman al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the foremost row and stand close together in the row."
"1813","1815 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1814","1816 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl and al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ashath, (h) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gestured to us to sit, so we sat; then he said: What prevents you from lining up as the angels line up before al-Rahman (the Most Merciful)? They said: And how do they line up, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They complete the first rows and align in the rows in ranks - or pack them tightly."
"1815","Chapter. 1817 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, (h) and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, both said: Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Some people will surely stop raising their gazes in prayer to the sky, or it will not return to them."
"1816","1818 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon them while they were raising their gazes, and said: Some people will surely stop raising their gazes to the sky in prayer, or it will not return to them."
"1817","1819 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people who raise their gazes to the sky in prayer will surely stop, or it will not return to them."
"1818","1820 - Salama ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, my maternal grandfather Khattab ibn Uthman narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Some people who raise their gazes to the sky in prayer will surely stop, or it will not return to them."
"1819","1821 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will surely stop raising their gazes in prayer, or it will not return to them."
"1820","1822 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw them raising their hands; he said: What is with them raising their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer."
"1821","1823 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while his Companions were seated, and said: Why do I see you in separate groups? Sufyan said: Meaning scattered circles."
"1822","Chapter. 1824 - Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawra al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some people who had raised their hands in prayer, and said: They have raised their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"1823","1825 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us in the mosque and saw them raising their hands in prayer; then he said: Why do I see them raising their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer."
"1824","1826 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them - I think he said: in the mosque - while they were raising their hands, and said: Why do I see you raising your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer."
"1825","1827 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and entered the mosque and saw the people raising their hands; then he said: Why do I see the people raising their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer."
"1826","1828 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some people who had raised their hands, and said: As if they are the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"1827","1829 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, then he mentioned the same."
"1828","1830 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the mosque and saw them seated in circles; then he said: Why do I see you in separate groups?"
"1829","1831 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while they were seated, and said: Why do I see you in separate groups?"
"1830","1832 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1831","Chapter. 1833 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The enemy seized the she-camel of a man from Banu Sulaym; then a Muslim man bought it, and its owner recognised it and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take it for the price for which he had bought it from the enemy, otherwise to leave it to him."
"1832","1834 - Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli al-Asbahani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir: that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a camel, and each of them established proof that it belonged to him, so he judged between them."
"1833","1835 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim ibn Tarafa, from Jabir ibn Samura, that two men disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a camel, and each of them established two witnesses that it belonged to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it between them."
"1834","Ubaydullah ibn al-Qibtiyya from Jabir ibn Samura. 1836 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Qibtiyya, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: When we prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would say: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you - and Misar gestured with his hand to his right and to his left - so he said: What is with these people raising their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Is it not enough for one of you - or one of them - to place his hand on his thigh, then greet his brother to his right and to his left?"
"1835","1837 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyayna, from Misar, from Ibn al-Qibtiyya, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: We would pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say with our hands: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you. So he said: What is with people casting up their hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? Is it not enough for one of you - or rather it is enough for one of you - to place his hand on his thigh, then greet his brother to his right and to his left?"
"1836","1838 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Misar, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Qibtiyya, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similar."
"1837","1839 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdha narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Ubaydullah, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed with us; when he gave the salutation, the people gestured with their hands right and left, and he saw them and said: What is with you turning your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? When one of you gives the salutation, let him greet the one to his right and the one to his left. Then when they prayed with him again, they did not do that."
"1838","1840 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Israil, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Qibtiyya, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we gave the salutation, we would gesture with our hands: Peace be upon you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at us and said: What is with you gesturing with your hands as if they are the tails of restive horses? When one of you gives the salutation, let him turn to his companions and not gesture with his hand."
"1839","1841 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdha narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Ubaydullah, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we sat with him; then he said: Islam will remain triumphant until there are twelve commanders or caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."
"1840","Abu Ishaq al-Sabii from Jabir ibn Samura. 1842 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abi Ishaq, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a bright moonlit night, wearing a red garment. He said: I kept looking at him and at the moon, and he was more beautiful in my eyes than the moon."
"1841","Abu Khalid al-Walibi from Jabir; his name is Harim ibn Hurmuz. 1843 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Walibi narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent - I and the Hour are like this of this: his middle finger and index finger."
"1842","1844 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was sent - I and the Hour are like these two."
"1843","1845 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abi Khalid, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent - I and the Hour are like these two."
"1844","1846 - Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal narrated to us, Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, (h) and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us - may Allah have mercy on him - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Israil, from Mansur, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent - I and the Hour are like these two."
"1845","1847 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid, from Jabir, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was sent - I and the Hour are like this of this."
"1846","1848 - Al-Qasim al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abi Khalid, from Jabir ibn Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was sent - I and the Hour are like these two."
"1847","1849 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain standing until twelve caliphs stand. Ismail said: I think - I conjecture - that my father said: All of them - the nation will unite upon them."
"1848","1850 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1849","1851 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"1850","1852 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, Abu Khalid informed us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who oppose this religion will not harm it, until twelve caliphs stand, all of them from Quraysh."
"1851","1853 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Three things I fear for my nation: seeking rain by the stars, tyranny of the ruler, and denial of divine decree."
"1852","1854 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The first one to shoot an arrow in the way of Allah was Sad."
"1853","1855 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubayda narrated to us, from his father, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The first one to shoot an arrow in the way of Allah was Sad."
"1854","1856 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubayda narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a detachment, and we routed (the enemy); Sad pursued a rider among them, who turned to him - and he saw his leg outside the stirrup - so he shot him with an arrow; and I saw the blood flowing as if it were a sandal-strap, then he (the rider) made his camel kneel."
"1855","1857 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Said ibn al-Mughira al-Sayyad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: We went out in a detachment, then he mentioned similar."
"1856","1858 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samura - or a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to graze sheep; then the sheep became too much, so he was among camels with a partner of his; then they hired the sister of Khadija; when they completed the journey, something remained due to them from her; so his partner would go to them demanding payment, saying to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Come along - and he would say: You go, for I am shy. Then once she said when he came to them: Where is Muhammad, why does he not come with you? He said: I said to him, and he claimed he is shy. She said: I have never seen a man more modest or more chaste in fulfilment. Then it fell into the heart of her sister Khadija, so she sent to him and said: Come to my father and propose to me from him. He said: Your father is a man of much wealth, and he will not do it. She said: Go, meet him and speak to him; then I shall suffice you - and come when he is intoxicated. So he did; he came to him and he married her to him. In the morning he sat in the gathering, and it was said to him: You have done well - you married Muhammad. He said: Did I do it? They said: Yes. So he stood and entered upon her and said: People say I married Muhammad, but I did not do it. She said: Do not deem your judgement foolish, for Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is such-and-such. She kept at him until he was pleased. Then she sent to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two uqiyyas of silver or gold and said: Buy a garment as a gift for me, and a ram, and such-and-such. So he did."
"1857","Jafar ibn Abi Thawr from Jabir ibn Samura. 1859 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution (wudu) from the meat of sheep? He said: If you wish, perform ablution; and if you wish, leave it. He said: May I pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes. He said: Should I perform ablution from camel meat? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No."
"1858","1860 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from his grandfather Jabir ibn Samura, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution from sheep meat? He said: If you wish, do so; and if you wish, do not do so. He said: Should I perform ablution from camel meat? He said: Yes. He said: O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No."
"1859","1861 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should ablution be performed from sheep meat? He said: If you wish, perform ablution; and if you wish, do not perform ablution. He said: May I pray in the sheepfold? He said: Yes."
"1860","1862 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak, he said: Jafar ibn Abi Thawr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Should I purify myself from camel meat? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: May I pray in the resting places of camels? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. He said: Should I purify myself from sheep meat? He said: If you wish, purify yourself; and if you wish, do not purify yourself. He said: May I pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes."
"1861","1863 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb and Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: May one pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No. It was said: Should ablution be performed from their meat? He said: Yes. He said: May one pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes. It was said: Should ablution be performed from their meat? He said: No."
"1862","1864 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution from camel meat, and not to perform ablution from sheep meat; and to pray in the sheepfolds, and not to pray in the resting places of camels."
"1863","1865 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ashath, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution from camel meat, and not to perform ablution from sheep meat; and to pray in the resting places of sheep, and not to pray in the resting places of camels."
"1864","1866 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (h) and Talib ibn Qurra al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, (h) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdillah ibn Mawhab, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir, he said: I was seated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was asked: Should we perform ablution from camel meat? He said: Yes - so perform ablution from camel meat. They said: May we pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No. They said: Should we perform ablution from sheep meat? He said: If you wish, perform ablution; and if you wish, do not perform ablution. They said: May we pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes."
"1865","1867 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Uthman ibn Abdillah ibn Mawhab, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, my grandfather Jabir ibn Samura informed me, he said: I was seated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, should we perform ablution from sheep meat? He said: If you wish, perform ablution; and if you wish, do not perform ablution. He said: Should I perform ablution from camel meat? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in the resting places of camels? He said: No. He said: May I pray in the resting places of sheep? He said: Yes."
"1866","1868 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, Jamil ibn al-Hasan al-Ataki narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Jafar al-Suwai, from his grandfather Jabir ibn Samura, he said: We would pray in the resting places of sheep, and would not pray in the resting places of camels; and we would perform ablution from camel meat, and would not perform ablution from sheep meat."
"1867","1869 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Jafar ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to fast Ashura, and would urge us and check upon us regarding it; then when Ramadan was made obligatory, he neither commanded us with it, nor forbade us from it, nor checked upon us regarding it."
"1868","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samura. 1870 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him."
"1869","1871 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, (h) and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him; and when Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1870","1872 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him."
"1871","1873 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanbah narrated to us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the way of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1872","1874 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Caesar is gone, there will be no Caesar after him; and when Kisra is gone, there will be no Kisra after him; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the way of Allah."
"1873","1875 - Bishr narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me twelve commanders - then he said a word I did not understand, so I asked my father: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1874","1876 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This affair will remain standing until there are twelve caliphs."
"1875","1877 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the lizard (dabb)? He said: A nation from the Children of Israel was transformed - I do not know which beasts they were transformed into; and I neither command it nor forbid it."
"1876","1878 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Simak and Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A band of Muslims will surely conquer the White (palace) of the family of Kisra."
"1877","1879 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi al-Kufi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Harun ibn Abi Burda narrated to us, my brother Husayn ibn Abi Burda narrated to me, from Qays, from Abd al-Malik, from Jabir ibn Samura and others, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is entrusted."
"1878","1880 - Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The woman travelling alone (al-zaina) will surely go out from Medina until she enters al-Hira, fearing none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1879","1881 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, (h) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydillah al-Halabi narrated to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Jabir ibn Samura, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in the garment in which I have intercourse? He said: Yes - unless you see something in it, then wash it."
"1880","Mabad al-Jadali from Jabir ibn Samura. 1882 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Asim ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Fitr narrated to us, from Abi Khalid al-Walibi and Mabad al-Jadali, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This affair will remain triumphant; those who oppose it will not harm it."
"1881","Al-Musayyib ibn Rafi from Jabir ibn Samura. 1883 - Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This affair will remain triumphant; those who oppose it will not harm it, until twelve commanders stand, all of them from Quraysh."
"1882","Simak ibn Harb from Jabir ibn Samura. Sufyan al-Thawri from Simak. 1884 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, (h) and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit between the two sermons on Friday and address standing; and his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate; and he would recite verses of the Quran upon the pulpit."
"1883","1885 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit in his place of prayer when dawn rose, until the sun rose bright."
"1884","Shuba ibn al-Hajjaj from Simak. 1886 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Samura about the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He would address standing, then sit a sitting, then stand."
"1885","1887 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would address standing, then sit a sitting, then stand."
"1886","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do after praying Fajr. He said: He used to sit in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"1887","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was staying at the house of Abu Ayyub. When food was brought and he ate from it, he would send the remainder to Abu Ayyub. Then food containing garlic was brought and he did not eat from it, and he sent it to Abu Ayyub, but Abu Ayyub did not eat from it since he saw no trace of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it. Then he came to him and asked him about it, saying: O Messenger of Allah, is it unlawful? He said: No, but I disliked it because of its smell. He said: Then I dislike what you dislike."
"1888","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The grey hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he combed his beard - I think he said, and oiled it - was not visible, but when he left it, it was visible."
"1889","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who said: He heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"1890","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He named Madinah Tabah."
"1891","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr Surahs like By the night when it covers and By the sun and its brightness, and the like, and in Fajr he recited something longer than that."
"1892","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: When the sun had declined, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Zuhr and recite something like By the night when it covers, and Asr likewise, and the other prayers likewise, except Fajr, for he would lengthen it."
"1893","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, meaning when it passed the meridian, and he prayed Asr about like your prayer."
"1894","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be twelve rulers. Then he said a word I did not understand, and the people said: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1895","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: A hairy, short, muscular man who had confessed adultery was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He turned him away twice, then ordered that he be stoned, and said: Every time we go out campaigning in the cause of Allah, one of you stays behind bleating like a billy-goat, granting one of these women a heap of milk. As for me, if any of you who does this is brought to me, I will make an example of him. Simak sometimes said: except that I will punish him severely."
"1896","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"1897","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, and Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah while we were witnesses. Then a horse was brought and held until he mounted it, and it began to prance with him while we hurried around him. A man beside Jabir ibn Samurah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many clusters of dates for Ibn al-Dahdah, hanging in Paradise."
"1898","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah while he was on a horse, trotting on it."
"1899","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many clusters of dates for Ibn al-Dahdah in Paradise."
"1900","Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A group of Muslims will conquer the white treasure of the family of Khosrau, or he said: that which is in the white palace."
"1901","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to me, Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had redness in the whites of his eyes. Shu'bah said: I said to Simak: What is redness of the eyes? He said in Persian: almond eyes."
"1902","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, both saying: Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, who said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah about the description of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He had redness in the whites of his eyes, a wide mouth, and lean heels."
"1903","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in Fajr something longer than that."
"1904","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: I found in my father's book in his handwriting, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"1905","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Ma'ibi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a stone that used to greet me before I was sent; indeed I know it."
"1906","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Asad narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and between his shoulders was something like a pigeon's egg: the seal of prophethood."
"1907","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father informed me, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: Boys used to pass by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); some he would wipe on one cheek and some on both cheeks. I passed by him and he wiped my cheek. He said: The cheek the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped was better than the other cheek."
"1908","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ali al-Bahili narrated to us, Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite poetry to one another while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listened."
"1909","Israel ibn Yunus, from Simak: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach on Friday standing, then sit without speaking, then stand and preach another sermon. Whoever tells you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached sitting has lied."
"1910","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call the adhan, then wait and not call the iqamah until, when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come out, he would call the iqamah when he saw him."
"1911","Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he sat in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"1912","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the prayers about like the prayer you pray today, but he would lighten; his prayer was lighter than your prayer. He would recite in Fajr al-Waqi'ah and similar surahs."
"1913","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of Muslims will conquer the treasures of Khosrau."
"1914","Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had thick hair and beard."
"1915","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: Ma'iz ibn Malik, a short man wearing only a waist-wrapper with no cloak, was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He spoke to him, though I do not know what he said to him as I was far from him with people between us. He said: Take him away. Then he said: Bring him back. He spoke to him while I could hear, though people were between us. Then he said: Take him away and stone him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and preached while I listened. He said: Every time we go out in the cause of Allah, one of them stays behind with bleating like a billy-goat's bleat, granting one of these women a heap of milk. By Allah, if any of them is brought to me, I will punish him severely."
"1916","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I saw the seal near his shoulder like a pigeon's egg, resembling his skin."
"1917","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, from Jabir, that they entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cushion on his left side."
"1918","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Israel, from Simak ibn Harb, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died. He said: He has not died. Then he came a second and a third time. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did he die? He said: He slaughtered himself with an arrowhead he had. So he did not pray over him."
"1919","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: There was no white hair on the head and beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a few hairs in the parting of his head; when he combed and oiled his beard it showed, and when he left it, it did not show."
"1920","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"1921","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will be twelve rulers. Then he said something I did not understand, so I asked the people, and they said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1922","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: A camel died at al-Harrah near some needy people, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to eat it."
"1923","From Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and began to drive away something in front of him. When he finished, we asked him, and he said: That was a devil who cast sparks of fire upon my feet to distract me from the prayer. Had I seized him, he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of Madinah gathered around him."
"1924","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Israel, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: It was said to Jabir: Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a sword? He said: No, rather like the sun and the moon."
"1925","Za'idah ibn Qudamah, from Simak: Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, both saying: Za'idah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"1926","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, who said: Jabir ibn Samurah said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his sermon were moderate."
"1927","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israel, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Fajr Qaf, by the Glorious Qur'an, and his prayer afterwards was light."
"1928","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach on Friday except standing. Whoever tells you he sat, declare him false, for he never did so. Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach, then sit, then stand and preach; he gave two sermons, sitting between them."
"1929","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"1930","Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from Simak: Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, both saying: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to me, saying: A man fell ill and cries were raised over him. His neighbor came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: He has died. He said: How do you know? He said: I saw him, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not died. The man returned and cries were again raised over him. His wife said: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him. The man said: O Allah, curse him. Then the man went and saw him: he had slaughtered himself with shears he had. He went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him he had died. He said: How do you know? He said: I saw him slaughter himself with shears he had. He said: Did you see him? He said: Yes. He said: Then I will not pray over him."
"1931","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, all saying: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, who said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, often. He would not rise from his prayer place where he prayed until the sun rose; when it rose he stood. He would remain silent at length. They would talk, taking up matters of the pre-Islamic age, laughing, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled."
"1932","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing, then sit, then stand and preach standing. Whoever informs you that he preached sitting or reclining has lied. By Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand times."
"1933","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars. I said to Jabir: Did you hear it yourself? He said: I heard it myself."
"1934","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will be twelve rulers. Then he said something I did not understand, so I asked all the people, and they said: He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1935","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, who said: I asked Jabir ibn Samurah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He would lighten it for them and did not pray the prayer of these people."
"1936","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Fajr Qaf, by the Glorious Qur'an, and the like."
"1937","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and began to drive away something in front of him. When he finished, we asked him, and he said: That was a devil who cast sparks of fire upon my feet to distract me from the prayer. He said: I drove him away, and had I seized him he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of Madinah gathered around him."
"1938","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to me, saying: Bowls used to be gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the house of Abu Ayyub, and he would send him the remainder of what he ate. A bowl came to him and he sent it back as it was, untouched. Abu Ayyub said to his family: Do not eat until I know why he left it. He said: He sought permission and entered, and said: Nothing used to come to us from you except that you ate from it, apart from this bowl; I do not know what is the matter with it. He said: There was garlic in it and I disliked its smell; yet there is no harm in it, only I disliked its smell. He said: Then I dislike what you dislike. He said: Then you know best."
"1939","Asbat ibn Nasr al-Hamdani, from Simak ibn Harb: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights."
"1940","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed on a festival day without adhan or iqamah."
"1941","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: When Ibn al-Dahdah died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed his funeral. When he was buried and finished with, a horse was brought; he mounted it and returned upon it."
"1942","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I prayed the first prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he went out to his family and I went out with him. The boys of Madinah met him and he began wiping the cheeks of each of them one by one. He said: He gestured and wiped my cheek, and I found his hand cool and fragrant, as though he had taken it out of a perfumer's box."
"1943","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Abi Hassan narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. Then he stood, entered his house, performed ablution, then came out to me and said: And upon you be peace, and upon you be peace."
"1944","Sharik ibn Abdullah al-Nakha'i, from Simak: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, and Abu Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: A she-camel died at al-Harrah beside a needy household of Banu Sulaym, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to eat it, and they ate from it through their winter, melting its fat. The wording is that of Ibn al-Asbahani's narration."
"1945","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: Bilal used to call the adhan for Zuhr when the sun declined, and he would sometimes delay the iqamah but not delay the adhan."
"1946","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times. His companions would recite poetry to one another and recall things from the pre-Islamic age, and he would sometimes smile along with them."
"1947","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was moderate and his sermon was moderate."
"1948","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hundred times; he never preached except standing, and he would sit one sitting."
"1949","Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: When we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each of us would sit wherever he reached."
"1950","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, and Abu al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a festival day; no adhan was called for him nor iqamah."
"1951","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I said to Jabir: Did you sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; he was long silent."
"1952","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi and Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah al-Juddi narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"1953","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: A man killed himself, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"1954","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) suffered wounds that pained him. He crawled to a horn in his sword, took an arrowhead, and killed himself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over him."
"1955","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Nakha'i Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: Bilal would call the adhan, then seek permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1956","Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Fajr and recited By the sun and its brightness and By the sky and the night-comer."
"1957","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the last Isha prayer."
"1958","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would not rise from his prayer place where he had prayed until the sun rose."
"1959","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me on the nights I was sent."
"1960","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, raising the narration, who said: I was shown Laylat al-Qadr then made to forget it; so seek it in the last ten nights. And he said: It is a night of wind, rain, and thunder."
"1961","Hammad ibn Salamah, from Simak: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: There was no white hair on the head and beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a few hairs in the parting of his head; when he oiled, the oil concealed them."
"1962","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, and Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Amr al-Waki'i narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching, saying: Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs. Then he said a word I did not understand. I said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"1963","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing."
"1964","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr By the sky with its constellations and By the sky and the night-comer, and the like."
"1965","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned Ma'iz and did not mention flogging."
"1966","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that Bilal used to call the adhan for Zuhr when the sun declined."
"1967","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"1968","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: They used to say Madinah and Yathrib, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, named it Tabah."
"1969","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who heard Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man was at al-Harrah with his wife. A man lost his camel and the man at al-Harrah found it and kept it with him, but the camel fell ill. His wife said to him: If only you slaughtered it and dried its meat and fat so we could eat them. He refused until it died. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Do you have anything else to live on? He said: No. He said: Then dry its fat and meat and eat them. The camel's owner came afterwards and said: Why did you not slaughter it? He said: I was shy before you."
"1970","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that when food was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ate from it, he would send the remainder to Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub would follow the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placing his fingers where he saw the Prophet's fingers. One day a tray was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he found in it the smell of garlic, so he did not eat from it and sent it to Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub saw no trace of the Prophet's fingers in it and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw no trace of your fingers. He said: I found in it the trace of garlic. He said: You sent me what you do not eat? He said: The angel comes to me."
"1971","Al-Waddah Abu Awanah, from Simak: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach standing, then sit a sitting in which he did not speak, then stand and preach another sermon upon his pulpit. Whoever tells you he saw him preach sitting, do not believe him."
"1972","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the prayers about like your prayer, and he would delay the night prayer a little after your prayer time, and he would lighten the prayer."
"1973","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A group of Muslims - or of believers - will conquer the treasure of the family of Khosrau that is in the white palace."
"1974","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He named Madinah Tabah."
"1975","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: A mule died belonging to a man, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling. Jabir claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to its owner: Do you have nothing that suffices you besides it? He said: No. He said: Go and eat it."
"1976","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars."
"1977","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I saw Ma'iz when he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): a short, muscular man. He testified against himself four testimonies that he had committed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps... He said: No, by Allah, the other had committed adultery. So he stoned him. Then he preached and said: Every time we go out in the cause of Allah, one of them stays behind with bleating like a billy-goat's bleat, granting one of these women a heap of milk. Indeed, if Allah gives me power over any of them, I will make an example of him on their account."
"1978","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned Ma'iz and did not mention flogging."
"1979","Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym, from Simak: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, all saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I prayed the Eid with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once or twice, without adhan or iqamah."
"1980","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he sat in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"1981","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the last Isha prayer."
"1982","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: I used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate."
"1983","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave two sermons, sitting between them, reciting the Qur'an and reminding the people."
"1984","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: When food was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would take from it then send the remainder to Abu Ayyub. Food containing garlic was gifted to him, and he sent it to Abu Ayyub without tasting anything of it. When Abu Ayyub saw no trace of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the food, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I left it only because of its smell. Abu Ayyub said: And I dislike what you dislike."
"1985","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to name Madinah Taybah. Abu Bakr said: Tabah."
"1986","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars. I said: Did you hear this yourself from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"1987","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices one of you, when he finishes his prayer, to place his hand on his thigh and greet his brother to his right, Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left likewise."
"1988","Sa'id ibn Simak ibn Harb, from his father: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Ta'i narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ta'i narrated to us, Ibn al-Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times in the mosque. His companions would sit reciting poetry to one another, and sometimes recall matters of the pre-Islamic age, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled along with them."
"1989","Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Simak ibn Harb: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach two sermons, sitting between them."
"1990","Malik ibn Mighwal, from Simak: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, both saying: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah. When he returned, a bareback horse was brought and he mounted it while we walked."
"1991","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah, a bareback horse was brought and he mounted it while we walked around him."
"1992","Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ash'ath, from Simak: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh al-Harrani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ash'ath, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walk with a funeral procession, and when returning he rode a bare horse wearing nothing but its bridle."
"1993","Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Simak: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me when I was sent."
"1994","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"1995","Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Simak: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, both saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: It is as if I am looking at the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): his locks reaching this place. And he struck with his hand upon his chest above his nipples."
"1996","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra' narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar informed me, Anbasah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two. And he pointed with his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"1997","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would remain silent at length; they would talk of pre-Islamic matters, laughing, and he would smile along with them."
"1998","Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Simak: Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjunani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ja'far ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: Jabir ibn Samurah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Qaf in Fajr prayer."
"1999","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjunani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ja'far ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preach except standing on Friday. He would preach, then sit, then stand and preach: he gave two sermons with a sitting between them."
"2000","Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Simak: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi and Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ziyad ibn Khuthaymah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd, and the distance between its two ends is like that between San'a' and Aylah; its pitchers are as though stars."
"2001","Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Simak: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand upon the pulpit and preach, then sit, then stand and preach, sitting between the two sermons."
"2002","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached on Friday, he would recite from the Book of Allah and remind the people."
"2003","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, and Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I used to pray the prayers with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); his prayer was moderate and his sermon was moderate."
"2004","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Fajr, would sit in his prayer place until the sun rose."
"2005","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will stand twelve rulers. Then he said a word, so I asked my father, and he said: All of them are from Quraysh."
"2006","Al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Hayy, from Simak: Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until he had prayed sitting."
"2007","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, the latter two saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I saw the seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like a pigeon's egg."
"2008","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih informed me, from Simak ibn Harb, Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to me, saying: We prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah, a man of the Ansar. When we finished with him, a man brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a stalwart horse, and he mounted it when returning from the funeral."
"2009","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak, who said: Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to me, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This affair will remain standing, a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"2010","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never preached sitting; he preached only standing."
"2011","Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Simak: Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah on any day rise from the place where he prayed Fajr until the sun rose; then he would rise."
"2012","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Anbasah, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: Did you mention poetry in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; we would mention verses in his presence, laughing, while he smiled."
"2013","Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah, from Simak: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not lengthen the admonition on Friday; it was only a few brief words."
"2014","Qays ibn al-Rabi' al-Asadi, from Simak: Al-Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr about like your prayer, and he used to pray Maghrib about like your prayer, and he used to delay Isha somewhat after your prayer. Bilal would delay Zuhr until the sun declined, never missing a single time. As for the iqamah, sometimes the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out and hasten it, and sometimes delay it."
"2015","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, both saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Jabir, who said: I said to him: Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; he was long silent. His companions would recite poetry before him and mention things from the pre-Islamic age, laughing, while he smiled along with them when they laughed."
"2016","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Surah, Abu Khalifah, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, all saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah upon a bare horse."
"2017","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, raising it, that he used to pray Fajr then sit until the sun rose."
"2018","Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The white palace of Khosrau will be conquered by a party of Muslims."
"2019","From Simak ibn Harb, who said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: His sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate."
"2020","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: Amin, Amin, Amin. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: O Muhammad, whoever reaches one of his parents and dies and enters the Fire, Allah casts him away; say Amin. So I said: Amin. He said: O Muhammad, whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and dies unforgiven and is entered into the Fire, Allah casts him away; say Amin. So I said: Amin. He said: And whoever you are mentioned before and he does not send blessings upon you, and dies and enters the Fire, Allah casts him away; say Amin. So I said: Amin."
"2021","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks."
"2022","Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Simak: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah al-Halabi narrated to us, all saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The shins of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were slender, and he would laugh only smiling. When I looked at him I would say: kohl-eyed, though he was not wearing kohl. The wording is that of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah's narration."
"2023","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not burst out laughing."
"2024","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached standing, then sat."
"2025","Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dabbi, from Simak: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Talut narrated to us, both saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights."
"2026","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Makkah there is a stone that greets me; indeed I know it when I see it."
"2027","Nasih Abu Abdullah, from Simak: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Nasih Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: A young man used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and hasten in his errands. He said: Ask me for a need. He said: Supplicate Allah, the Exalted, for me for Paradise. He said: He raised his head, breathed, and said: Yes, but help me with abundant prostration."
"2028","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Nasih Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buries three children and is patient over them and seeks reward, Paradise becomes due for him. Umm Ayman said: Or two? He said: And whoever buries two and is patient over them and seeks reward, Paradise becomes due for him. Umm Ayman said: Or one? He said: He fell silent, or held back. He said: I heard Umm Ayman: Whoever buries one and is patient and seeks reward, Paradise will be his."
"2029","Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that all the doors of the mosque be closed except the door of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, just enough for me alone to enter and exit. He said: I was not commanded anything of that. So he closed them all except the door of Ali, though he would sometimes pass through while in major impurity."
"2030","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to discipline his child is better for him than to give half a sa' in charity to the poor every day."
"2031","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Subayh al-Asadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: When the people of Quba asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to build a mosque for them, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Let one of you stand and mount the she-camel.' So Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and mounted her and urged her but she did not rise, so he came back and sat down. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and mounted her and urged her but she did not rise, so he came back and sat down. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: 'Let one of you stand and mount the she-camel.' So Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood, and when he placed his foot in the stirrup the camel sprang up with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Ali, loosen her rein, and build at the limit of her roaming, for she is commanded.'"
"2032","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar and said: 'Amin, Amin, Amin.' Then he said: 'Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and said: O Muhammad, whoever reaches one of his parents...' and he mentioned the hadith."
"2033","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): 'You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.'"
"2034","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, who will carry your banner on the Day of Resurrection? He said: 'Who is fit to carry it except the one who carried it in this world: Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him).'"
"2035","Abdan ibn Ahmad ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): 'Who is the most wretched of Thamud?' He said: The one who hamstrung the she-camel. He said: 'Then who is the most wretched of this ummah?' He said: Allah knows best. He said: 'Your killer.'"
"2036","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): 'You are a man left behind as a successor, and you will be killed, and this will be dyed from this' - his beard from his head."
"2037","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out in the morning of the day of al-Fitr until he had eaten seven dates."
"2038","Abdan narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: There was no adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor any iqama, on the two Eids."
"2039","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Asad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Before the Hour there will be liars.'"
"2040","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen delivering the sermon except standing."
"2041","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: A man of Banu Sulaym who lived in the Harra with his children used to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, and in the evening he would return to his family. A she-camel of his died, and his wife said to him: Feed us its meat, for we are in dire need. He said: No, by Allah, not until I inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came to him and told him the news. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Do you have anything that would spare you from it?' He said: No. He said: 'Go and eat it.' So they melted its fat and sufficed themselves with its meat for the rest of their year."
"2042","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There will be twelve commanders.' Then he spoke something I did not hear, and the people claimed that he said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2043","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, from Amr, from Simak, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not rise from the place in which he prayed until the sun had risen."
"2044","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So-and-so has died. He said: 'He has not died' - saying it three times."
"2045","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, from Amr, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl containing garlic, and he sent it to Abu Ayyub - and he mentioned the hadith."
"2046","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, from Amr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray the morning prayer and gestured with his hand - and he mentioned the hadith."
"2047","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us - both saying: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: Ma'iz - a short man wearing an izar - was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining on a cushion. When he was brought to him he drew the cushion aside and spoke to him, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reddened, and he knew that he had angered him. So he gestured with his hand that they stone him. Then he sent a man after him and spoke to him briefly, then said: 'Take him away and stone him.' So the people rose. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Now then, whenever we go out in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind bleating like the bleating of a billy-goat, granting one of those women something. Indeed, if Allah gives me power over any of them, I shall surely make an example of him.'"
"2048","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Umar ibn Musa narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go out for the funeral of Thabit ibn al-Dahdah riding a blaze-faced horse with white feet, with no saddle on it, with the people around him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted, then sat until it was over, then stood and mounted his horse, then set off riding."
"2049","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, from Jabir, who said: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to address the people sitting on the minbar, then belie him. Jabir said: And I am a witness that he used to address standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the last sermon. He said: So I said: How was his sermon? He said: Speech with which he admonished the people and recited verses from the Book of Allah, and it was moderate, and his prayer was moderate, with something like al-Shams wa Duhaha and al-Sama wa al-Tariq - except the morning prayer and the noon prayer, for Bilal used to call the adhan when the sun declined, and sometimes he delayed the iqama a little and sometimes he hastened it; as for the adhan, he never missed its time. And al-Asr was about like what you pray, and al-Maghrib about like what you pray, and the last Isha he used to delay it a little beyond your prayer."
"2050","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ata, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the prayers about like your prayers. He used to pray al-Zuhr when the sun declined, and he used to recite in the dawn prayer Qaf wa al-Quran al-Majid and Ya-Sin and the like."
"2051","Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Budayl narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: We prayed an obligatory prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he clasped his hands together in the prayer. When he finished the prayer we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: 'No, except that Satan wanted to pass in front of me, so I strangled him until I felt the cold of his tongue on my hand. And by Allah, were it not for what my brother Sulayman had already been given before me, he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of Madinah circled around him.'"
"2052","Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir, that a man of Jarmaqan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned the hadith."
"2053","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the obligatory prayer as a middle, balanced prayer, neither lengthening it nor shortening it, and he used to delay the night prayer (al-Atama)."
"2054","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khuzayma al-Basri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I saw the seal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was at his shoulder like a dove's egg."
"2055","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mihran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit."
"2056","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us - all saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Aidh ibn Nusayb, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samura say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his finger while in prayer, and when he gave the salam I heard him say: 'O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know.'"
"2057","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me - both saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Khaythama narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Said al-Hamdani, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'This ummah will remain upright, its affair sound and dominant over its enemy, until twelve caliphs from them pass, all of them from Quraysh. Then when he returned to his house, Quraysh came to him and said: Then what will happen? He said: Then there will be harj (killing).'"
"2058","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from al-Nadr ibn Salih, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I was with my father while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and he said: 'You will remain in good as long as twelve commanders rule over you.' I said to my father: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say just now like that? My father said: He said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2059","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abda ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'My ummah will remain upon the truth, dominant, until there are over them twelve commanders, all of them from Quraysh.'"
"2060","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Hamdani narrated to us, who said: I heard Ziyad ibn Ilaqa and Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrating from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him say: 'There will be after me twelve commanders.' Then he lowered his voice, so I said to my father: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There will be after me twelve commanders' - so what did he lower his voice for? He said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2061","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Simak and Ziyad ibn Ilaqa and Husayn, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There will be after me twelve commanders.' Then he spoke something I did not hear, so I asked my father what he said, and he said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2062","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Sahl said: And Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tamim, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The enemy seized a she-camel belonging to a Muslim man, and a Muslim man bought it. Its owner recognized it and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take it for the price for which he had bought it from the enemy, otherwise to leave him alone with it."
"2063","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, al-Rabi' ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Jabir ibn Samura narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as the brilliant star is seen on the horizon of the sky. And Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed are they.'"
"2064","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind to look at the place of the seal. When he looked at me, he cast off his cloak, and I looked at it."
"2065","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There will rise after me twelve commanders.' Then he spoke something I did not hear, so I asked the people and I asked my father what he said - and he was closer to him than me - and he said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2066","Al-Hasan ibn Allawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'This matter will neither pass nor end until twelve caliphs pass.' Then he spoke something I did not understand. I said to my father: What did he say? He said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2067","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2068","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There will be after me twelve commanders.' Then he spoke and it was unclear to me, so I asked the one next to me, and he said: 'All of them from Quraysh.'"
"2069","Muhammad ibn al-Layth and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2070","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us - both saying: Abu Usama narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Siyah, Imran ibn Rabah narrated to me, from Ali ibn Umara, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I was in the gathering of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), along with Samura and Abu Umama, and he said: 'Foul speech and deliberate foulness are in no way part of Islam, and the best of people in Islam are the best of them in manners.'"
"2071","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Huraysh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymuna, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing on the minbar, saying: 'Twelve custodians from Quraysh; the enmity of whoever opposes them will not harm them.' He said: Then I turned behind me, and there were Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and my father among some people, and they confirmed the hadith for me as I had heard it."
"2072","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Malik al-Ghubari narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abu Muhammad al-Suwai - of the descendants of Jabir ibn Samura - narrated to me, from his uncle Harb ibn Khalid, from Maysara the freedman of Jabir ibn Samura, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'May Allah curse whoever returns to bedouin life after migration; may Allah curse whoever returns to bedouin life after migration; may Allah curse whoever returns to bedouin life after migration - except during fitna, for the desert is better than residence during fitna.'"
"2073","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, from Abu Tamima al-Hujaymi, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord?' They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: 'They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row.'"
"2074","Mas'ada ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mu'adh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from Jabir ibn Usama al-Juhani, who said: I went to the market and met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his Companions. I asked them where he intended to go, and they said: He is marking out a mosque for your people. So I returned and found my people standing, and I said: What is the matter with you? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked out a mosque for us with his foot, and set up a piece of wood in the qibla direction, planting it in it."
"2075","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us - both saying: Abu Murra al-Harith ibn Murra ibn Mujja'a al-Yamami narrated to us, Nafis narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jabir - meaning al-Abdi - who said: I was among the delegation of Abd al-Qays whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lodged, though I was not of them; I was only with my father. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the dubba, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat."
"2076","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr say: Jabir ibn Abi Tariq - his son narrated a hadith from him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This is what Ibn Numayr said: Jabir ibn Abi Tariq."
"2077","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Za'ida, who said: I saw Hakim ibn Jabir dyeing with yellow."
"2078","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us - both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: I visited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and there was dubba (pumpkin) with him. I said: What are you doing with it? He said: 'We increase our food with it.'"
"2079","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir al-Ahmasi, from his father, who said: I visited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw dubba with him. I said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'We increase the food of our household with it.'"
"2080","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: I visited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this dubba was with him. I said: What is this? He said: 'This dubba, this pumpkin - we increase our food with it.'"
"2081","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: I saw pumpkin with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What is this? He said: 'We increase our food with it.'"
"2082","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Farah al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jabir ibn Tariq, who said: Our family used to prepare pumpkin, and Jabir ibn Tariq said to me: I have seen this with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: 'Something with which we increase our food.'"
"2083","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mahbub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: I saw cut pumpkin before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What are you doing with this? He said: 'We increase our food with it.'"
"2084","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: In the book of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', concerning the naming of those who witnessed with Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him): 'And Jabr ibn Anas, a Badri, of Banu Zurayq.'"
"2085","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us - both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Dahtham ibn Qurran narrated to us, Nimran ibn Jariya al-Hanafi narrated to us, from his father, who said: Some people brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a reed hut. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Hudhayfa to judge between them, and he judged for the one towards whom the binding faced. When he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, he said: 'You are right' - or 'You did well.'"
"2086","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Dahtham ibn Qurran narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Dinar the freedman of Jariya ibn Zafar, from Jariya ibn Zafar, that two brothers had a fence in the middle of a house. They died, each leaving offspring, and the offspring of each claimed the fence as his to the exclusion of the other. They brought the dispute to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman with them. He judged the fence for the one whom the knots of the binding were found facing. Then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of that, and he said: 'You are right' - or 'You did well.'"
"2087","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Dahtham ibn Qurran narrated to us, Nimran ibn Jariya al-Hanafi narrated to us, from his father, who said: A man struck a man with a sword on his forearm, not at a joint, and sought justice against him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He judged blood-money for him, while the struck man wanted retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'May Allah bless you in it' - and he did not judge retaliation for him."
"2088","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Asad ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, from Dahtham ibn Qurran, from Nimran ibn Jariya, from his father, that a man cut off the hand of a man from the middle of the forearm, and he disputed with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He judged for him five thousand dirhams and said: 'Take it; blessed for you in it.'"
"2089","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Asad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Dahtham, from Nimran ibn Jariya, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Take fresh water for the head.'"
"2090","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Abi Za'ida, from Amir al-Sha'bi, who said: Six of the Ansar collected the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu Zayd, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Abu al-Darda, Sa'd ibn Ubada, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b. And in the hadith of Zakariya: Jariya ibn Mujammi' ibn Jariya had recited it all except a surah or two."
"2091","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from his uncle - or another - who mentioned Jariya ibn Qudama, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word in Islam that I may perhaps grasp, and be brief. He said: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2092","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word that will benefit me, and be brief, that I may retain it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated it to him several times, saying: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2093","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say to me a word, and be brief, that I may grasp it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated it to him, and he said: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2094","Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word that will benefit me, and be brief, that I may grasp it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated it to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2095","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, that his uncle came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word, and be brief, that I may retain it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated it to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2096","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Jariya ibn Qudama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2097","Al-Abbas ibn Humran al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Talha ibn Qays, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, from a cousin of his, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something in Islam that will benefit me. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then I repeated it to him, and he did not add to that."
"2098","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from a cousin of his, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word, and be brief, that I may grasp it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then I returned to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2099","Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, who said: I witnessed al-Ahnaf ibn Qays narrating to his uncle - and his uncle was Jariya ibn Qudama - while he was with Ibn Abbas. He said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word that will benefit me, and be brief, that I may grasp it. He said: 'Do not get angry.' Then he repeated, and he said: 'Do not get angry.'"
"2100","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from a cousin of his of Banu Tamim, from Jariya ibn Qudama, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word - then he mentioned the like of it."
"2101","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle of his of Banu Tamim called Jariya ibn Qudama, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Say to me a word, and be brief - then he mentioned the like of it."
"2102","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle of his of Banu Tamim, from Jariya ibn Qudama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2103","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Ahnaf, from Jariya ibn Qudama, from a cousin of his of Banu Tamim who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned the like of it."
"2104","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, al-Ahnaf ibn Qays narrated to me, from a cousin of his called Jariya ibn Qudama, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word in Islam, and be brief, that I may grasp and retain it - then he mentioned the like of it."
"2105","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, from Urwa, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariya ibn Qudama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2106","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zarbi ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: When the people of Bahrain came, and al-Jarud came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he rejoiced at him and brought him near and close."
"2107","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, all saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abdullah ibn Babay, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that al-Jarud Abu al-Mundhir informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stray animals, and he said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2108","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Jarud al-Abdi, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire, so do not go near it.'"
"2109","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from al-Jarud al-Abdi, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about barren stray camels that came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the believer is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2110","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2111","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us - both saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2112","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yazid the brother of Mutarrif, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2113","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yazid the brother of Mutarrif, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2114","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2115","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.' And Said did not mention Yazid ibn Abdullah."
"2116","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us - all saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Ala, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire.'"
"2117","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayya narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi of Jadhima Abd al-Qays narrated to us, al-Jarud narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire, so do not go near it.'"
"2118","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, who said: Two hadiths I narrated have been preserved for me: Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi narrated to me, from al-Jarud, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and riding animals were scarce. The people discussed the riding animals among themselves, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, we pass by a herd of riding camels in a ravine, so may we use their backs? He said: 'No; the stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire; the stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire; the stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire' - three times. He said: 'And the lost item you find: announce it, then do not conceal it nor hide it. If you find its owner, deliver it to him; otherwise it is but the wealth of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, which He directs to whomever He wills.'"
"2119","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi narrated to us, from al-Jarud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire, so do not go near it.' And he said: 'The stray and the lost item you find: announce it, and do not conceal nor hide it. If it is recognized, deliver it; otherwise it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"
"2120","Muhammad ibn Azhar al-Ubulli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Maymun al-Ataki narrated to us, Hilal ibn Hiqq narrated to us, from Abu Mas'ud al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from his brother Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and riding animals were scarce. We discussed what would suffice us of riding animals. We said: A herd we come upon in a ravine, and we use their backs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The stray of the Muslim is the kindling of the Fire' - three times - 'so do not go near it.' And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Concerning the stray you find: do not hide it nor conceal it. If it is recognized, deliver it; otherwise it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.'"
"2121","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about drinking standing - and he forbade him."
"2122","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, and Abu Khalifa and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us - both saying: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud ibn al-Mu'alla, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade a man to drink standing."
"2123","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Hilal ibn Haqq."
"2124","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from al-Jarud al-Abdi, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a religion; is it for me, if I leave my religion and enter your religion, that Allah will not punish me in the Hereafter? He said: 'Yes.'"
"2125","Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Ibn Sirin, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2126","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Nasr ibn Khalid al-Nahwi narrated to us, Haddab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Durays narrated to us, from al-Haytham, from al-Jarud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever seeks the world by the deed of the Hereafter, his face will be effaced, his mention blotted out, and his name recorded in the Fire.'"
"2127","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hisn ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyash al-Sulami narrated to us, who said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Jaz narrate: Hibban ibn Jaz informed me, from Jaz, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a captive who had been with him - of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whom they had taken captive while they were polytheists; then they accepted Islam, and they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with that captive. He clothed Jaz in two cloaks, and Jaz accepted Islam in his presence. Then he said: 'Enter upon Aisha; she will give you two cloaks from the cloaks with her.' So he entered upon Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and said: May Allah brighten you - choose for me from these cloaks with you two cloaks, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me from them in two cloaks. She said - stretching out a long siwak of arak - she said: Take this and take this. And the women of the Arabs at that time were not seen."
"2128","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to me, that Asad ibn Wada'a narrated to him that a man called Jaz came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my family angers me - with what shall I punish them? He said: 'Pardon.' Then he said it a second time, until he said it three times. He said: 'If you punish, then punish according to the sin, and avoid the face.'"
"2129","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those killed on the day of al-Yamama of the Ansar, then of Banu Jahjaba: Jaz ibn Malik ibn Amir ibn Hudayr."
"2130","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those martyred on the day of al-Yamama of the Ansar, then of al-Aws, then of Banu Amr ibn Awf: Jaz ibn Malik."
"2131","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu Khunas ibn Sinan ibn Ubayd ibn Adi ibn Ghanm ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj: Jubbar ibn Sakhr ibn Umayya ibn Khansa ibn Ubayd ibn Adi ibn Ghanm."
"2132","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqaba of the Ansar: Jabbar ibn Sakhr."
"2133","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, who said: Jabbar ibn Sakhr died in Madinah in the year thirty, at the age of sixty-two."
"2134","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, who said: Abdullah ibn Rawaha only assessed the produce for the people of Khaybar for one year, then he was struck on the day of Mu'ta. Then Jabir ibn Sakhr ibn Khansa was the one the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send after Ibn Rawaha, and he would assess their produce."
"2135","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Jabbar ibn Sakhr, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he placed me at his right."
"2136","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Zur'a ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, from Jarhad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Cover your thigh, for the thigh is awrah.'"
"2137","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Abu al-Zinad, from Ibn Jarhad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I had my thigh uncovered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Cover it, for it is part of the awrah.'"
"2138","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, both saying: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zur'a ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad al-Aslami narrated to me, from his grandfather Jarhad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while his thigh was uncovered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Cover your thigh, O Jarhad, for the thigh is awrah.'"
"2139","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Abu al-Zinad, from Ibn Jarhad, from Jarhad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw him with his thigh uncovered and said: 'Cover it, for the thigh is awrah.'"
"2140","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shababa narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Ibn Jarhad, from Jarhad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he had his thigh uncovered, and said: 'Cover it, for it is part of the awrah.'"
"2141","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Zur'a ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, from his father, who said: Jarhad was of the people of al-Suffa. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat with us while my thigh was uncovered, and said: 'Do you not know that the thigh is awrah?'"
"2142","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: I read to Abdullah ibn Nafi': Malik informed us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Zur'a ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad al-Aslami, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat with him - and he was of the people of al-Suffa - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his thigh uncovered and said: 'Cover your thigh, for the thigh is awrah.'"
"2143","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Zur'a ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, from his father - and he was of the people of al-Suffa - that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat with us one day while my thigh was uncovered, and said: 'Cover yourself; do you not know that the thigh is awrah?'"
"2144","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Zur'a ibn Muslim ibn Jarhad narrated to me, from his grandfather Jarhad, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was in the mosque wearing a cloak with my thigh uncovered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Cover your thigh, O Jarhad, for the thigh is awrah.'"
"2145","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tha'laba ibn Sawa narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jarhad, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he had his thigh uncovered, and said: 'Cover it, for it is part of the awrah.'"
"2146","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'The thigh of a man is part of the awrah.'"
"2147","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abdullah ibn Jarhad al-Aslami, that he heard his father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The thigh of the Muslim man is part of his awrah.'"
"2148","Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Awza'i say: The thigh in the mosque is awrah, and in the bathhouse it is not awrah."
"2149","Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Harmala ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him, from Sufyan ibn Farwa, from one of the sons of Jarhad, from Jarhad, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with food before him. Jarhad extended his left hand to eat, for his right was injured. He said: 'Eat with the right.' He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is injured. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blew on it, and he never complained of it until he died."
"2150","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us - all saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to me, Ubayd ibn Salman al-Agharr narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jahjah al-Ghifari, that he came with a group of his people seeking Islam. They attended al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he gave the salam he said: 'Let each man take the hand of his companion.' None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and me - and I was huge and tall, with none preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I finished it off, until he milked seven goats for me and I finished them off. Then a pot of food was brought, and I finished it off. Umm Ayman said: May Allah starve whoever starved the Messenger of Allah this night. He said: 'Hush, O Umm Ayman; he ate his provision, and our provision is upon Allah.' In the morning they came early, and he gathered with his Companions, and each man told of what had been brought to him. Jahjah said: Seven goats were milked for me and I finished them off, and a pot of food and I finished it off. They prayed al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'Let each man take the hand of his companion.' None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and me - and I was huge and tall, with none preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I was satisfied and full. Umm Ayman said: O Messenger of Allah, is this not our guest? He said: 'Yes.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'He ate tonight in the intestine of a believer, whereas before that he ate in the intestine of a disbeliever. The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.'"
"2151","Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, concerning the naming of those martyred on the day of al-Taif: Julayha ibn Abdullah ibn Muharib ibn Nashib ibn Sa'd ibn Layth."
"2152","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umara narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended the expedition of Tabuk, he said to Jadd ibn Qays: 'Would you like the daughters of the yellow ones (Romans)?' He said: Grant me leave and do not tempt me. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And among them is he who says: Grant me leave and do not tempt me.'"
"2153","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khallad Abu Umayya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Jahm ibn Muti', from Ali ibn Jahm al-Balawi, from his father, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday, and he asked us who we were. We said: We are Banu Abd Manaf. He said: 'You are Banu Abdullah.'"
"2154","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Mulayh ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mina, from Judan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever offers an excuse to his brother and he does not accept it, upon him is like the sin of the collector of unjust taxes.'"
"2155","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, that he came from al-Tur and met Jamil ibn Basra al-Ghifari. Jamil said to him: Had I met you before you went to al-Tur, you would not have gone to it - and he mentioned the hadith."
"2156","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from Jamil al-Ghifari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis.'"
"2157","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Umayya ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, that Abu Basra Jamil ibn Basra met Abu Hurayra while he was coming from al-Tur, and said: Had I met you before you went to it - I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The livers of riding camels are only wearied to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and al-Aqsa Mosque.'"
"2158","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Basra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of the Messenger, and al-Aqsa Mosque.'"
"2159","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, who said: I met Abu Hurayra and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque.'"
"2160","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: 'I am riding to the Jews; whoever of you sets out with me, do not greet them first. If they greet you, say: And upon you.' When we came to them, they greeted us, and we said: And upon you."
"2161","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Basra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'We are going tomorrow to the Jews; when you meet them and they greet you, say: And upon you.' We met them, they greeted us, and we said: And upon you."
"2162","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I am setting out tomorrow to the Jews, so do not greet them first. If they greet you, say: And upon you.'"
"2163","Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym, from Abdullah ibn Hubayra, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day the Asr prayer at al-Mukhammas, then turned, and said: 'This prayer was presented to those before you, but they were negligent of it and abandoned it. Whoever of you prays it, his reward will be doubled twofold. And there is no prayer after it until the witness rises.' Al-Layth said: And I heard it from Khayr ibn Nu'aym with this chain."
"2164","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us - both saying: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ibn Hubayra narrated to us, that Abu Tamim al-Jayshani Abdullah ibn Malik narrated to him that he heard Abu Basra al-Ghifari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Asr at al-Mukhammas - a valley of some of their valleys - then said: 'This prayer was presented to those before you and they abandoned it. Indeed, whoever prays it, his reward will be doubled for him. And there is no prayer after it until you see the witness' - and it is the star."
"2165","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ibn Hubayra narrated to me, that Abu Tamim al-Jayshani Abdullah ibn Malik informed him that he heard Amr ibn al-As say: A man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has added a prayer for you, so pray it between the Isha prayer and the dawn prayer: al-Witr, al-Witr. Indeed it is Abu Basra al-Ghifari.' Abu Tamim said: I and Abu Dharr were sitting, and Abu Dharr took my hand, and we set out to Abu Basra and found him at the door by the house of Amr. Abu Dharr said to him: O Abu Basra, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has added a prayer for you, so pray it between Isha and the dawn prayer: al-Witr, al-Witr? He said: Yes. He said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes."
"2166","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Hubayra, from Abu Tamim, from Abu Basra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has added a prayer for you, so guard it, and He made its time between Isha and Fajr, and it is al-Witr.'"
"2167","Harun ibn Mallul al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, who said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Kulayb ibn Dhuhl narrated to him, that Ubayd ibn Jabr said: I boarded a ship from al-Fustat with Abu Basra, a Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he brought his lunch near, then said to me: 'Come near.' I said: Are we not still among the houses? Abu Basra said: 'Have you turned away from the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?'"
"2168","Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Kulayb ibn Dhuhl al-Hadrami, from Ubayd ibn Jabr, that he traveled with Abu Basra al-Ghifari in Ramadan. When they departed from al-Fustat, he called for food while we could still see al-Fustat. I said to him: You eat, while if we wished we could still see al-Fustat? He said: 'Do you turn away from the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions?' And he broke his fast."
"2169","Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu Hani al-Khawlani, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: 'I asked my Lord for four things: He gave me three and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to unite my ummah upon misguidance, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to destroy them by years of famine as He destroyed the nations before them, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to give an enemy from besides them power over them, and He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to divide them into sects nor make them taste one another's might, and He withheld it from me.'"
"2170","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Rafi' ibn Salama ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated to me, from Ju'ayl al-Ashja'i, who said: I went out on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his campaigns, riding a lean, weak mare of mine, and I was at the rear of the people. He caught up with me and said: 'Move on, O rider of the horse.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, she is lean and weak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised a whip that was with him, struck her with it, and said: 'O Allah, bless him in her.' He said: I found myself holding her head back lest she outpace the people. He said: And I sold from her offspring for twelve thousand."
"2171","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us - both saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Hudhafa al-Azdi, from Junada al-Azdi, who said: I visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of al-Azd on Friday. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited us to food before him, and we said: We are fasting. He said: 'Did you fast yesterday?' We said: No. He said: 'Will you fast tomorrow?' We said: No. He said: 'Then break your fast.' Then he said: 'Do not fast Friday alone.'"
"2172","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Hudhafa al-Azdi, from Junada al-Azdi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"2173","Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Hudhayfa al-Azdi, from Junada al-Azdi, that they came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - eight men, he being the eighth of them - on Friday. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for food and said to a man: 'Eat.' He said: I am fasting. He said to another: 'Eat.' He said: I am fasting - until he asked them all. He said: 'Did you fast yesterday?' They said: No. He said: 'Will you fast tomorrow?' They said: No. Then he commanded them to break their fast."
"2174","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him, that Hudhayfa al-Bariqi narrated to him, that Junada ibn Abi Umayya al-Azdi narrated to him, that they entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - eight men, he being the eighth of them - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought food near to them on a Friday. He said: 'Eat.' They said: We are fasting. He said: 'Did you fast yesterday?' They said: No. He said: 'Will you fast tomorrow?' They said: No. He said: 'Then break your fast.'"
"2175","Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi' al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ismail ibn al-Yasa' narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to me, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-San'ani, that Junada al-Azdi led some people in prayer. When he stood for the prayer, he turned to his right and said: Are you pleased? They said: Yes. Then he did the like to his left. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Whoever leads a people in prayer while they dislike him, his prayer does not pass beyond his collarbone.'"
"2176","Junadah b. Malik: Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah, Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi narrated to us: from Ubaydah b. al-Aswad, from Qasim b. al-Walid, from Mus'ab b. Ubaydullah b. Junadah, from his father, from his grandfather Junadah b. Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are from the deeds of the people of ignorance which the people of Islam will not abandon: seeking rain by the stars, disparaging lineage, and wailing over the dead."
"2177","Junadah b. Jarad al-Ghaylani: Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Awn b. al-Hakam b. Sa'd al-Bahili narrated to us: Ziyad b. Quray' of Banu Ghaylan b. Jawah narrated to us, from his father, from Junadah b. Jaradah of Banu Ghaylan b. Jawah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with camels which I had branded on their noses, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Junadah, did you find no limb to brand except the face; ahead of you is retaliation. He said: Its matter is up to you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Bring me something that has no brand. So I brought him a young camel and a hiqqah, and I placed the branding iron on the neck, and he kept saying: Move it back, move it back, until it reached the thigh. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Brand with the blessing of Allah. So I branded them on their thighs; their zakah was two hiqqahs, and they were ninety."
"2178","Jarmuz al-Hujaymi: Muhammad b. Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Ar'arah informed us: Abd al-Samad b. Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Ubaydullah b. Hawdhah narrated to us, from Jarmuz al-Hujaymi, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you not to be one who curses frequently."
"2179","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Warith b. Abd al-Samad b. Abd al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ubaydullah b. Hawdhah al-Quray'i narrated to me, saying: a man narrated to me that he heard Jarmuz al-Hujaymi say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you not to be one who curses frequently."
"2180","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Habib b. Nudbah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah b. Hawdhah al-Quray'i, from a shaykh, from Jarmuz, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2181","Ja'dah al-Jushami: Muhammad b. Abdus narrated to us: Ali b. al-Ja'd narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us: Abu Isra'il, the freedman of Banu Jusham b. Mu'awiyah, informed me, saying: I heard Ja'dah, a man of theirs, narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: They brought a man to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one intended to kill you. He said to him: You need not fear, you need not fear; had you intended that, you would not have been given power over me."
"2182","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki' informed us, from Shu'bah: Abu Isra'il al-Jushami narrated to us, from a shaykh of theirs called Ja'dah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that a man had a dream concerning him, so he sent for him and he came and narrated it to him; and he had a large belly, so he pointed with his finger at his belly and said: Had this been elsewhere than this, it would have been better for you."
"2183","Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Rahawayh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Isra'il, from a shaykh of theirs called Ja'dah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with a large belly, so he pointed with his finger at his belly and said: Had this been elsewhere than this, it would have been better for you."
"2184","Ja'dah b. Hubayrah: Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ja'dah b. Hubayrah, who said: A freedman of Banu Abd al-Muttalib who prayed and did not sleep and fasted and did not break fast was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I pray and I sleep, and I fast and I break fast; and for every deed there is zeal, and for every zeal there is a lull; so whoever's lull is toward the Sunnah is guided, and whoever's is toward other than that has gone astray."
"2185","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abdullah b. Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ja'dah b. Hubayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the rest are the vilest."
"2186","al-Qasim b. Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ja'dah b. Hubayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then the one that follows it, then the rest are the vilest."
"2187","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Rawh b. Ubadah narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Mujahid, that Ja'dah b. Hubayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me three things: wearing a gold ring, wearing qassi garments, and using the mitharah."
"2188","Jafshish al-Kindi: Ibrahim b. Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Isma'il b. Amr al-Bajali narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Salih narrated to us, from his father, from al-Jafshish al-Kindi, who said: Some people of Kindah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You are of us, and they claimed him. He said: We do not slander our mother nor disavow our father; we are the children of al-Nadr b. Kinanah."
"2189","Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Hayyan b. Bishr al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya b. Adam narrated to us: Ali b. Hayy narrated to me, from his father: al-Jafshish al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Of whom are you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: We are the sons of al-Nadr b. Kinanah; we do not slander our mother nor disavow our father."
"2190","Jabalah b. Harithah al-Kalbi, brother of Zayd b. Harithah: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami and Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Minjab b. al-Harith narrated to us: Ali b. Mushir informed us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani: Jabalah b. Harithah narrated to me, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, send my brother Zayd with me. He said: He is that one; if he goes with you I will not prevent him. He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will never prefer anyone over you. He said: So I considered my brother's judgment better than my own judgment."
"2191","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: al-Walid b. Amr b. Sukayn narrated to us: Amr b. al-Nadr narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid informed us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Jabalah b. Harithah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"2192","Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: Muhammad b. Sa'id b. al-Asbahani narrated to us, and Ahmad b. Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Tufayl narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Jabalah b. Harithah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out to raid, he gave his weapon to Ali or Usamah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2193","Ahmad b. Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Tufayl narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Jabalah b. Harithah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you go to your bed, recite: Say, O disbelievers, until you pass its end, for it is freedom from polytheism."
"2194","Jabalah b. al-Azraq: Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Salih narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Salih narrated to me, from Rashid b. Sa'd, from Jabalah b. al-Azraq, who was of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed beside a wall with many stones, praying Zuhr or Asr; when he sat in the two rak'ahs, a scorpion came out and stung him and he lost consciousness, so the people recited ruqyah over him; when he recovered he said: Allah healed me, and it was not by your ruqyah."
"2195","Jabalah b. Amr, brother of Abu Mas'ud: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: And in the hadith of Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi' concerning the naming of those who were present with Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: Jabalah b. Amr of Banu Bayadah, a Badri."
"2196","Jabalah b. Tha'labah al-Ansari of Banu Bayadah, a Badri: al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: And in the hadith of Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi' concerning his naming of those who were present with Ali b. Abi Talib: Jabalah of Banu Bayadah, a Badri."
"2197","Jahsh al-Juhani: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali b. Abd al-A'la al-Muharibi and Hannad b. al-Sari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. al-Harith, from Abdullah b. Jahsh, from his father al-Juhani, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a desert area where I pray, so command me a night to come down to the mosque and pray in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come down on the night of twenty-three."
"2198","Jahr Abu Abdullah: Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith b. Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us: Zakariyya b. Yahya b. Khallad al-Minqari narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Umar al-Sadusi narrated to us: Uthman b. Abd al-Rahman al-Madani narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah b. Jahr, from his father Jahr, who said: I recited behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he finished he said: O Jahr, let your Lord hear and do not make me hear."
"2199","Jufaynah: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Amr b. Awn narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Uraynah al-Urani, from Jufaynah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a letter to him and he patched his bucket with it; his daughter said to him: You took the letter of the chief of the Arabs and patched your bucket with it. So he fled and took all little and much that belonged to him, then he came afterwards as a Muslim, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: See what you find of your property before the division of the shares, take it."
"2200","Jahimah Abu Mu'awiyah al-Sulami: Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us: Sufyan b. Habib narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Talhah b. Yazid b. Rukanah, from Mu'awiyah b. Jahimah, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulting him about jihad, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have parents? I said: Yes. He said: Stay with them, for Paradise is beneath their feet."
"2201","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, and Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Sa'd b. Abd al-Hamid b. Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: al-Abbas b. al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us: al-Qasim b. Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Yazid b. Shajarah, from Jidar, a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and our enemy met us; he stood and praised Allah and glorified Him, then said: O people, you have come to be between green and yellow and red, and in the baggage is what is in it; so when you meet your enemy, then forward, forward; for there is none who charges in the path of Allah except two of the wide-eyed houris hasten to him; and if he is martyred, then with the first drop that falls of his blood Allah Almighty expiates every sin from him, and they wipe dust from his face, saying: I am now for you, and he says: I am now for you both."
"2202","Junayd b. Sab' - also said to be Habib b. Siba', he is Abu Jum'ah, whose hadith I have brought out in the chapter of Ha: Abu al-Zinba' Rawh b. al-Faraj narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Abdullah Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Hujr b. Khalaf narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah b. Awf say: I heard Junayd b. Sab' say: I fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the first part of the day as a disbeliever, and I fought with him in the last part of the day as a Muslim; and concerning us was revealed: And were it not for believing men and believing women. He said: We were nine persons, seven men and two women."
"2203","Jarir b. Abdullah al-Bajali, his kunyah Abu Abdullah, also said Abu Amr: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim b. Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Aswad b. Shayban narrated to us: Ziyad b. Abi Sufyan al-Bajali narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Jarir narrated to us, saying: Abu Abdullah, meaning Jarir, went out early to the Kunasah to buy a beast from it."
"2204","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Jarir b. Ayyub narrated to us: a shaykh of Banu Sulaym narrated to me, saying: I said to Jarir: O Abu Amr."
"2205","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Yunus narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, who said: I saw Jarir dyeing his beard yellow."
"2206","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Hannad b. al-Sari narrated to us: al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Malik b. Umayr say: I saw Jarir dyeing with yellow and saffron."
"2207","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Mansur al-Kalbi narrated to us, saying: Sulaym Abu al-Hudhayl narrated to me, saying: I saw Jarir b. Abdullah dyeing his head and beard black."
"2208","Of his reports: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad b. al-Sa'ib, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: Jarir b. Abdullah appeared, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall appear before you the best of Dhu Yaman, upon him the touch of an angel. Then Jarir b. Abdullah appeared."
"2209","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Isma'il narrated to us: Sulayman b. Ibrahim b. Jarir narrated to us, from Aban b. Abdullah al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, who said: Ali b. Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jarir is of us, Ahl al-Bayt, outwardly and inwardly. He said it three times."
"2210","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ja'far b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan, known as Ibn al-Tall, narrated to us: Ahmad b. Bishr narrated to us, from Ibn Shubrumah, from al-Sha'bi, that Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, fought Mihran in single combat and killed him; his waistband was valued at thirty thousand; and whoever fought a man in single combat and killed him, his spoil belonged to him; so they wrote to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umar said: This is not of the spoil that is given; it is not of the weapons nor of the horses, and he did not award it to him as extra share but made it booty."
"2211","Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid: Amir narrated to us, from Jarir: That Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, led the people in prayer and something came out of a person, so he said: I adjure its doer to perform ablution and repeat his prayer. Jarir said: Do you adjure everyone who heard it to perform ablution and repeat the prayer? He said: What an excellent thing. I said: May Allah reward you with good. So he commanded them with that."
"2212","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Mansur al-Kalbi narrated to us: Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us: Sulaym Abu al-Hudhayl narrated to us, saying: I was a companion at the door of Jarir b. Abdullah; he would come out riding a mule of his with his boy mounted behind him."
"2213","Ahmad b. Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad b. al-Awwam, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: A man may clothe himself while naked, meaning thin garments."
"2214","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali b. Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, who said: Jarir and al-Ash'ath b. Qays gathered at a funeral, and al-Ash'ath put Jarir forward and he prayed over it."
"2215","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, who said: Jarir, Adi b. Hatim and Hanzalah the scribe went out from Kufah to Qarqisiya, saying: We shall not remain in a town in which Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, is reviled."
"2216","Anas b. Malik from Jarir: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ar'arah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yunus b. Ubayd, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas b. Malik, who said: I accompanied Jarir and he would serve me, though he was older than Anas; and Jarir said: I saw what the Ansar did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I see none of them except I honor him."
"2217","Qays b. Abi Hazim from Jarir, chapter on the virtue of Jarir: Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me except he smiled."
"2218","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, saying: I heard Jarir b. Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw me at all except he smiled in my face."
"2219","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Waki' and Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor ever saw me except he smiled in my face."
"2220","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abu Hatim al-Sijistani the grammarian narrated to us: Abu Jabir Muhammad b. Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me except he smiled."
"2221","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas narrated to us: Abu Mas'ud narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir b. Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me except he smiled."
"2222","Chapter clarifying the disbelief of the misguided Jahmiyyah by the seeing of the Lord Almighty on the Resurrection: Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us, and Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to us, saying: Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us: Qays narrated to us, saying: Jarir said to me: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the full moon, and he said: You shall see your Lord as you see this moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then recite this verse: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"2223","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, saying: I heard Qays b. Abi Hazim narrating from Jarir, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the full moon, and he said: You shall see your Lord as you see the moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then recite this verse: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"2224","Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibn Numayr, Abu Usamah and Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: You shall be presented before your Lord and see Him as you see this moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then recite: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"2225","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Hammad b. Usamah, Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah and Waki' narrated to us, saying: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he looked at the moon on the night of fourteen, and said: You shall see your Lord as you see this; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so. Then he recited this verse: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"2226","al-Hasan b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2227","Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Ata al-Khuza'i narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You see your Lord as you see the moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him."
"2228","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad b. Sulayman Luwayn narrated to me: Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2229","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab b. Abd al-Hakam al-Warraq narrated to me: Yahya b. Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2230","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us: Asad b. Musa narrated to us: Sufyan b. Uyaynah and Abdah b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall see your Lord; you will not be wronged in seeing Him, as you look on the night of the full moon."
"2231","Musa b. Harun narrated to us: Khalaf b. Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abu Shihab al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: You shall see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection plainly as you see this; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so. Then he recited: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset. Abu al-Qasim said: In this hadith is the added wording of his saying plainly; Abu Shihab is alone in it, and he is a precise memorizer of the trustworthy Muslims."
"2232","Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan and Marwan b. Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the fourteenth of a month, and he said: Do you see this moon? You shall see your Lord as you see this moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so whoever of you is able, let him not be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset."
"2233","Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad b. Amr al-Qalawri narrated to us: Yahya b. Kathir Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Shu'bah and Abdullah b. Uthman narrated to us, saying: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night and our gazes rose and we began looking at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: You look at your Lord as you look at this; you will not be wronged in seeing Him; so if you are able not to be overcome regarding two prayers, then do so: a prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset."
"2234","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Abd al-A'la b. Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us: Mu'tamir b. Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrating from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said to us: You shall see your Lord as you see this; you will not be wronged in seeing Him."
"2235","Ahmad b. Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us: Usayd b. Asim narrated to us: Amir b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Anbasah, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the moon rose, and he said: You shall look at your Lord; you will not be wronged in seeing Him, as you look at the moon."
"2236","Chapter: Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2237","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar narrated to us: Sufyan and Marwan b. Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2238","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not show mercy to one who does not show mercy to people."
"2239","Ahmad b. Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Muhammad b. Rafi' al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Mus'ab b. al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Dawud al-Ta'i, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2240","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya b. Muti' al-Shaybani narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Malik b. Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2241","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Mas'ud Ahmad b. al-Furat narrated to us: Abu Usamah and Ya'la b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2242","Chapter: Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, hearing Qays b. Abi Hazim, saying: I heard Jarir say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2243","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir and Abdah b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2244","Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2245","al-Miqdam b. Dawud narrated to us: Asad b. Musa narrated to us: Yazid b. Ata narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2246","al-Miqdam b. Dawud narrated to us: Asad b. Musa narrated to us: Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2247","Abu Bakr b. Sadaqah narrated to us: Muhammad b. Khalid b. Khali al-Himsi narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Salamah al-Awsi narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan al-Hamdani, he is Ali b. Salih, narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2248","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jumhur b. Mansur narrated to us: Isma'il b. Mujalid narrated to me, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey."
"2249","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Mas'ud Ahmad b. al-Furat narrated to us: Abu Usamah and Ya'la b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2250","Chapter: Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah, and it was a house in Khath'am called the Ka'bah of al-Yamaniyyah. So I went out with one hundred and sixty horsemen of Ahmas, and they were horsemen; and I could not stay firm on horses, so he struck my chest until I saw the trace of his fingers on my chest, and said: O Allah, make him firm and make him a guide, rightly guided. So he went to it and broke it and burned it, and sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informing him; the messenger of Jarir said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I left it like a mangy camel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blessed the horses of Ahmas and its men five times."
"2251","Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan and Marwan b. Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, hearing Qays b. Abi Hazim, hearing Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not suffice me against Dhu al-Khalasah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who cannot stay firm on horses. So he struck my chest and said: O Allah, make him a guide, rightly guided. He said: So I went out to it with fifty of my people and burned it with fire; then I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I left it like a hairless camel. So he supplicated for Ahmas, its horses and its men, three times."
"2252","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: I could not stay firm on horses, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he struck his hand on my chest until I saw the trace of his hand on my chest, and said: O Allah, make him firm and make him a guide, rightly guided. So I never fell from a horse afterwards."
"2253","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir and Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jarir, will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah, a house of Khath'am called the Ka'bah of al-Yamaniyyah. So I set out with one hundred and fifty horsemen of Ahmas; and I could not stay firm on horses, so I mentioned that to him, and he struck my chest until I saw the trace of his fingers on my chest, then said: O Allah, make him firm and make him a guide, rightly guided. So I went and prevailed over them and burned it with fire; and Jarir sent a man called Abu Artah as a bearer of glad tidings to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I saw it like a mangy camel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blessed the horses of Ahmas and the men of Ahmas three times."
"2254","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas narrated to us: Abu Mas'ud Ahmad b. al-Furat narrated to us: Ya'la b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2255","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Bishr narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There remains of the idols of ignorance only Dhu al-Khalasah."
"2256","Chapter: Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall enter upon you through the door a man of the best of Dhu Yaman, upon his face the touch of an angel. Then Jarir entered."
"2257","Chapter: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abdullah b. Idris narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I was in Yemen with Dhu Kala' and Dhu Amr, and I began informing them about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Dhu Amr said: O Jarir, if your companion is as you mention, his term came three days ago. Then a man appeared to us and we said: What is the news? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has passed away and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, has succeeded him, and the people are righteous. Then we returned, and they said: Convey peace to your companion. Then Dhu Amr said: O Jarir, you shall remain righteous so long as when a leader perishes, a leader stands; but when it comes to swords, you shall be kings, approving the approval of kings and angering the anger of kings."
"2258","Chapter: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik b. Isma'il narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Isma'il b. Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, and Ahmad b. al-Qasim al-Jawhari narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Sayf b. Harun narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: We pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the like of what the women pledged: whoever of us dies without committing any of them, Paradise is guaranteed for him; whoever dies having committed something of them and the hadd was applied to him, it is his expiation; and whoever of us dies having committed something of them and it was concealed for him, his reckoning is upon Allah."
"2259","Chapter: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us, and Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: al-Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, saying: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Isma'il, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah al-Bajali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever resides with the polytheists, the protection is free of him."
"2260","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar and Muhammad b. Salih b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Bilal narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from al-Hajjaj b. Artah, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The protection is free of one who resides with the polytheists in their lands."
"2261","Chapter: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab b. al-Harith narrated to us: Husayn b. Umar narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is deprived of his two precious ones, I compensate him for them with Paradise."
"2262","Muhammad b. Abdus b. Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment to Khath'am, and some of them sought protection by prostration, but killing was hastened among them; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered for them half the blood-money and said: I am free of every Muslim who resides among the polytheists. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why? He said: Their two fires should not be visible to each other."
"2263","Chapter: al-Qasim b. Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Maymun narrated to us: Salih b. Umar narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army to Khath'am; when the horsemen overcame them, they sought protection by prayer, but a man of them was killed; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned for them half the blood-money because of their prayer, and said: I am free of every Muslim with a polytheist."
"2264","Chapter: Muhammad b. Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us: Muhammad b. Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Abi Khalaf narrated to us, saying: Husayn b. Umar narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, I came to him to pledge allegiance to him, and he said: For what have you come, O Jarir? I said: I have come to become Muslim at your hands. He said: So he called me to the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and to establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, and believe in the decree, its good and its evil. He said: Then he cast his cloak to me, then turned to his Companions and said: When the noble of a people comes to you, honor him; and the wording is of the hadith of al-Hadrami."
"2265","Muhammad b. Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us: Muhammad b. Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us: Husayn b. Umar al-Ahmasi narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Iblis has despaired of being worshipped in the land of the Arabs."
"2266","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya b. Muti' al-Shaybani narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Malik b. Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: Uyaynah b. Hisn entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there was a man with him, and he asked for drink and water was brought, and he screened it and drank; he said: What is this? He said: Modesty and faith, you were given them and we were denied them."
"2267","Chapter: Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Yahya b. Muti' al-Shaybani narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Malik b. Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, that Uyaynah b. Hisn entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while A'ishah was with him, and said: Who is this sitting beside you? He said: A'ishah. He said: Shall I not give up to you one better than her, meaning his wife. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go out and seek permission. He said: It is an oath upon me not to seek permission from a Mudari. A'ishah, may Allah have mercy on her, said: Who is this. He said: This is a fool who is followed."
"2268","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Hisham b. Ammar narrated to us: Khalid b. Yazid narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a supplication that is not heard, a heart that does not humble itself, and a soul that is not sated."
"2269","Chapter: Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Hisham b. Ammar narrated to us: Marwan b. Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provisions himself in this world, it benefits him in the Hereafter."
"2270","Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ali b. Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us: Sahl b. Amir narrated to us: Yahya b. Salamah b. Kuhayl narrated to us, from Bayan and Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he raised his gaze to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah, what tribulations are sent down upon them like the sending of rain?"
"2271","Chapter: Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Abdus b. Kamil al-Siraj narrated to us: al-Hasan b. al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, saying: Khalaf b. Tamim narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Ibrahim b. al-Muhajir, saying: I heard Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrating from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: Allah Almighty gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"2272","Chapter: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Mada al-Missisi narrated to us: Khalaf b. Tamim narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Ibrahim b. Muhajir, saying: I heard Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir b. Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty gives for gentleness what He does not give for roughness; and when Allah loves a servant He gives him gentleness; there is no household deprived of gentleness except they have been deprived."
"2273","al-Hasan b. Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us: Muhammad b. Hisham b. Abi Khayrah al-Sadusi narrated to us: Umar b. Ali narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The transgressor in charity is like its withholder."
"2274","Chapter: Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Ali b. Mansur al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Waki'i narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Uyaynah, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and property except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah Almighty."
"2275","Chapter: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Ziyad al-Rusafi narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Yahya b. Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Ubaydah b. Abi al-Safar narrated to us, saying: Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Ask the people to be silent. Then he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"2276","Ahmad b. Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad b. al-Awwam, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, who said: Jarir b. Abdullah said: Do they enumerate the dead, or he said: the family of the dead, after he is buried? - Isma'il doubted - I said: Yes. He said: We used to count it as wailing."
"2277","Abdan b. Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad b. Mani' narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: They used to consider the gathering of the dead person's family and the preparing of food as wailing."
"2278","Chapter: Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ziyad b. Ayyub narrated to us: Yahya b. Abd al-Malik b. Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: It used to be said: The first glance a man does not own, but one who persists in looking stealthily."
"2279","Abu Hanifah Muhammad b. Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Abu al-Ash'ath Ahmad b. al-Miqdam narrated to us: Ubayd b. al-Qasim narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: When was revealed: And your Lord would not destroy the towns unjustly while their people are reformers, he said: And their people deal justly with one another."
"2280","Chapter: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal, Abdan b. Ahmad and Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan b. Qaza'ah narrated to us: Buhlul b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, who said: A man asked Jarir about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: We used to wipe in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: Before the revelation of al-Ma'idah or after the revelation of al-Ma'idah? He said: I became Muslim only after the revelation of al-Ma'idah."
"2281","Chapter: Muhammad b. Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamdani narrated to us: Muhammad b. Musaffa narrated to us: Yahya b. Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us: Dawud b. al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset, he said: Sunrise is the Fajr prayer, and before sunset is the Asr prayer."
"2282","Chapter: Ali b. Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Atiyyah narrated to us: Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter; and the freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"2283","Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad b. Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us: al-Walid b. al-Qasim narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah and not having shed unlawful blood shall enter through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes."
"2284","Bayan b. Bishr from Qays from Jarir: Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us: Bayan narrated to us, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me except he laughed."
"2285","Abu Yazid Yusuf b. Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us: Sa'id b. Mansur narrated to us, and Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never screened himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me except he laughed."
"2286","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to me: al-Husayn b. Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah: Bayan al-Bajali narrated to us, from Qays: Jarir narrated to us, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us on the night of the full moon and said: You shall see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection as you see this moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him."
"2287","Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us, and Abdan narrated to us: Wahb b. Baqiyyah narrated to us, and al-Husayn b. Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: In ignorance there was a house called Dhu al-Khalasah, called the Yamanite Ka'bah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Will you relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah? He said: So I went to it with one hundred and fifty horsemen of Ahmas, and I broke it and killed whom I found at it; then I came to him and informed him, and he supplicated for us and for the Ahmasiyyin."
"2288","Ali b. Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ali b. Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us: Sahl b. Amir al-Bajali narrated to us: Yahya b. Salamah b. Kuhayl narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid and Bayan, from Qays, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he raised his gaze to the sky and said: Glory be to Allah, what tribulations are sent down upon them like the sending of rain?"
"2289","Aslam b. Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us: Tamim b. al-Muntasir narrated to us: Ali b. Asim narrated to us, from Bayan b. Bishr, from Qays, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2290","Mujalid b. Sa'id from Qays: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami and Ahmad b. Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, saying: Umar b. Isma'il narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Bayan, Isma'il and Mujalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us on the night of the full moon and looked at the moon and said: You look at your Lord on the Day of Resurrection as you look at this moon; you will not be wronged in seeing Him."
"2291","Ibrahim b. Jarir from Qays from Jarir: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Jarir, from Qays, from Jarir, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"2292","Ibrahim b. Jarir from Jarir: Ahmad b. Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us: Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud b. Abd al-Jabbar, who said: I went out with Ibrahim b. Jarir at a funeral, and he was riding; when we reached the graveyard, a snake came out, and Ibrahim said: My father narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it out of fear of it is not of me."
"2293","Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Sa'id b. Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us: Dawud b. Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Jarir, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the owner of the right: Take your right in chastity, complete or incomplete."
"2294","Tariq b. Abd al-Rahman from Qays b. Abi Hazim from Jarir: Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim b. Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hasan b. Umarah, from Tariq b. Abd al-Rahman, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There remains of the idols of ignorance only the house of Dhu al-Khalasah; who will volunteer for Allah and His Messenger? Jarir said: I will. And seven hundred volunteered with him, all of Ahmas; the people were surprised only by the forelocks of horses; they killed and destroyed the house; and they wrote to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with glad tidings, informing him that nothing remained of it except like a mangy camel or like a scabby camel; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell prostrate, then said: O Allah, bless Ahmas in its horses and men."
"2295","Zayd b. Wahb al-Juhani from Jarir: Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2296","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us: Ya'qub b. Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Fudayl b. Iyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Jarir b. Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2297","Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Rahawayh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2298","Abu Husayn Muhammad b. al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Abi Mu'awiyah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2299","Muhammad b. Qada al-Jawhari narrated to us: Ali b. Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Zayd b. Wahb, from Jarir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever shows mercy to people, Allah shows mercy to him."
"2300","Abu Wa'il Shaqiq b. Salamah from Jarir b. Abdullah, Salamah b. Kuhayl from Abu Wa'il: Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter; and the freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"2301","Muhammad b. Amr b. Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih b. Sa'id, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Shaqiq b. Salamah, from Jarir b. Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged allegiance, he pledged upon the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, hearing and obeying Allah and His Messenger, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2302","Muhammad b. Amr b. Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih b. Sa'id, from Salamah, from Shaqiq, from Jarir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, he said: In the name of Allah, in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah; do not misappropriate, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill children."
"2303","Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated to us: Ali b. Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar b. al-Qasim narrated to us, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Shaqiq, from Jarir, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his armies, he said: In the name of Allah, in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah; do not misappropriate, do not mutilate, and do not kill an infant."
"2304","Asim b. Bahdalah from Abu Wa'il from Jarir: Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah b. Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Jarir, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me, for you know the condition better than I. He said: I pledge you to worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist."
"2305","Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Ibn A'ishah narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me, for you know better. He said: Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and disavow the disbeliever."
"2306","Ibrahim b. Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Shayban b. Farrukh narrated to us: Ikrimah b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me, for you know the condition better than I, then extend your hand that I may pledge to you. He said: Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist."
"2307","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muslim b. Sallam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2308","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter; and the freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"2309","Abdullah b. Muhammad b. al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Mas'ud Ahmad b. al-Furat narrated to us: Muhammad b. Sa'id b. Sabiq narrated to us: Amr b. Abi Qays narrated to us, from Asim b. Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter; and the freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another."
"2310","Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Asim b. Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: Some desert people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing patched woolen garments, and they asked him; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged the people to charity, but they were slow with it until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then a man of the Ansar came with a piece of gold ore and cast it; then the people followed one another in charity until joy was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he said: Whoever institutes a good practice and it is acted upon after him, he shall have its reward like its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever institutes an evil practice and it is acted upon, upon him shall be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2311","al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he urged the people to charity until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then a man of the Ansar came with gold and cast it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); joy was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he said: Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, he shall have its reward and like the reward of whoever acts upon it, not diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, upon him shall be its burden and like the burden of whoever acts upon it, not diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2312","al-Hakam b. Utaybah from Abu Wa'il: Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il Shaqiq b. Salamah, from Jarir b. Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"2313","Sulayman al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Jarir: al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid b. Salih narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge me and stipulate upon me, for you know better. So he extended his hand and he pledged him, saying: Do not associate anything with Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and separate from the disbeliever."
"2314","Ahmad b. Ali al-Jarudi narrated to us: Usayd b. Asim narrated to us: Amir b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ya'qub al-Qummi, from Abu Rib'i, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq b. Salamah, from Jarir, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, extend your hand that I may pledge to you, and take upon me, for you know the condition better than I. He said: I pledge you to not associate anything with Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist."
"2315","Mansur b. al-Mu'tamir from Abu Wa'il from Jarir: Ahmad b. Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Salih b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us: Uthman b. Umar narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stipulated upon me to worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2316","Abu Nukhaylah al-Bajali from Jarir: Mu'adh narrated to us: Ali b. al-Madini narrated to us, and Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us: my father narrated to me, and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Nukhaylah al-Bajali, who said: Jarir said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was pledging people, and said: O Messenger of Allah, extend your hand that I may pledge to you. He said: How shall you pledge to me? He said: You pledge me to worship Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist."
"2317","Zadhan Abu Umar from Jarir, chapter: Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Salamah b. Abd al-Rahman, from Zadhan, from Jarir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"2318","Ali b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"2319","Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Musa b. Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us: Husayn b. Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"2320","Abu Amir Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Suri narrated to us: Sulayman b. Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Isma'il b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Dawud b. Isa, from Amr b. Qays, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"2321","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated: from Dawud ibn Isa, from Amr ibn Qays, from Uthman Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lahd (side niche in the grave) is for us, and the shaqq (straight trench in the grave) is for others."
"2322","Zakariyya al-Saji narrated to us: Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated; both said: Sharik narrated: from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"2323","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated (ha), and Abu Husayn narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated; both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated: from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"2324","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated: from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"2325","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated: from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about Islam, so he said: You bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and you establish the prayer, and give the zakah, and fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House, and you love for people what you love for yourself, and you dislike for people what you dislike for yourself."
"2326","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated: from Abu Hamzah al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"2327","Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hayyaji narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated: Abu Hamzah al-Thumali Thabit ibn Said narrated: from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadhan, from Jarir, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on our mounts from Madinah while they were eating date stones; a figure appeared before him and he said: This is a man who has had no contact with food. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) quickened his pace and we quickened with him, and there was a young youth whose lips had lolled from eating tree bark. He asked him: From where have you come? He said: I seek Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him. He said: I am Muhammad, I am the Messenger of Allah. He said: Peace be upon you, guide me to Islam, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and you affirm what has come from Allah. He said: I affirm. He said: And you establish the prayer. He said: I affirm. He said: And you fast Ramadan. He said: I affirm. He said: And you perform Hajj to the House. He said: I affirm. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away. Jarir said: And we crowded around him when he began describing Islam to him, looking to see where his description would end. Then he turned away and we turned away, then the foreleg of his young camel fell into rat holes and his neck broke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned and said: Bring me the man. We found him with his neck bent and he had died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and looked at him, then turned his face away from him, and said: Carry him to the water. So we washed him and shrouded him and embalmed him, then he said: Dig for him and make a lahd grave, for the lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others. And he sat at his grave not speaking to us about anything, then he said: Shall I not tell you the story of this man? He is of those who did little and were rewarded much, of those about whom Allah Almighty said: Those who believed and did not mix their faith with wrongdoing. I turned away from him while two angels were stuffing the fruits of Paradise into his mouth."
"2328","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Zadhan, from Jarir, that a man entered Islam and was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, then the hoof of his camel entered a jerboa hole and it threw him and he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon him and said: He did little and was rewarded much. And he said: The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"2329","Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shuabah informed us: from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghudani, he heard al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the runaway slave: No prayer is accepted from him until he returns to his masters."
"2330","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated: from Mansur, al-Shaabi narrated to me that he heard Jarir ibn Abd Allah saying: Any slave who flees from his masters has disbelieved until he returns to them. Mansur said: By Allah, he did say it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I do not wish it to be reported from me in marfu form."
"2331","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated: from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the zakah collector return while he is pleased with you."
"2332","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated: Zaidah narrated: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated: Amir al-Shaabi narrated to me, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the zakah collector return while he is pleased with you."
"2333","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me (ha), and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us: my grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated; both said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated: Amir narrated: from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the zakah collector return while he is pleased with you."
"2334","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated: Wuhayb narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the zakah collector comes to you, let him not leave you except while he is pleased with you."
"2335","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Mujalid, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the zakah collector comes to you, let him not depart except with pleasure."
"2336","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the zakah collector return when he returns while he is pleased."
"2337","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Ismail ibn Ulayyah and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the zakah collector comes to you, let him leave you while he is pleased with you."
"2338","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated: Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Let the zakah collector leave you while he is pleased."
"2339","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated: from Dawud, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let the zakah collector return from you while he is pleased with you."
"2340","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us: Said ibn Sulayman narrated: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated: from Dawud, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon establishing the prayer, and giving the zakah, and sincere advice to every Muslim. Al-Shaabi said: And Jarir was intelligent, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, as much as I am able."
"2341","Ubayd al-Ijli and al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated: Ishaq ibn al-Rabi al-Usfuri narrated: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir al-Shaabi, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no possessor of kinship ties whose relative comes to him asking him for surplus wealth that Allah gave him, and he withholds from him, except that a serpent from Hell called Shuja will be brought out for him on the Day of Resurrection, licking its lips, and he will be collared with it."
"2342","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi al-Kufi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruwasi narrated: from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave joins the land of the enemy, his blood has become lawful."
"2343","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated: from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a slave flees to the enemy, the covenant of protection is absolved from him."
"2344","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ali narrated: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated: Israil narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him."
"2345","Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated (ha), and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated; both said: Sharik narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so seek forgiveness for him."
"2346","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated: from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek forgiveness for al-Najashi."
"2347","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Sharik narrated: from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave flees to the land of the enemy, the covenant of protection is absolved from him."
"2348","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Thalabah narrated: my father narrated: Sharik narrated: from al-Shaybani, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so seek forgiveness for him."
"2349","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated: Sufyan narrated: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and Mujalid narrated: from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and hearing and obeying, and establishing the prayer, and giving the zakah, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2350","Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated: Abu Dawud narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the zakah collector comes to you, let him not depart from you except while he is pleased."
"2351","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated: Umar ibn Ali narrated: from Ismail, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."
"2352","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Sayyar, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: Upon hearing and obeying, so he prompted me to say: As much as I am able, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2353","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Jarir narrated: from Mughirah, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let the zakah collectors not depart except with pleasure."
"2354","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman narrated: Jarir narrated: from Mughirah, from Abu Wail and al-Shaabi, both said: Jarir said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I said: I pledge allegiance to you upon hearing and obeying in what I love and dislike. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can you do that, O Jarir? Or can you bear that? Say: As much as I am able. He said: I said: As much as I am able. He said: So he took my pledge, along with sincere advice to the Muslim."
"2355","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman narrated: Jarir narrated: from Mughirah, from Amir, he said: Jarir used to narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a slave flees, no prayer is accepted from him, and if he dies he dies a disbeliever. Then a slave boy of Jarir fled, so he seized him and struck his neck. Abu al-Qasim said: Its meaning is that he disbelieved and joined the land of war."
"2356","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Khalid narrated: from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Firas, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him."
"2357","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated: from Mujalid, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a slave flees, the covenant of Allah and His Messenger is absolved from him."
"2358","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Abu Usamah narrated: from Mujalid, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave flees, the covenant of protection is absolved from him."
"2359","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yahya narrated: from Mujalid, from Amir al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the zakah collector comes to you, let him not leave you except while he is pleased."
"2360","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated: from Mujalid, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the zakah collector not return from you except while he is pleased."
"2361","Abu Usamah al-Daqqaq al-Basri narrated to me: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated: Sawrah ibn al-Hakam narrated: Abd Allah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated: from al-Shaabi, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, performing Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"2362","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated: Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated: from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, performing Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"2363","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated: Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated: from Amir, from Jarir, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, so he said: Stretch out your hand, O Jarir. He said: Upon what? He said: Upon submitting your face to Allah, and sincere advice to every Muslim. Jarir grasped it, and he was a sensible man, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, as much as I am able. So it became a concession for the people after him."
"2364","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated: Dawud al-Awdi narrated: from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a slave flees and joins the enemy, and dies while he is a disbeliever."
"2365","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Israil narrated: from Jabir, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Please your tax collectors and your zakah collectors."
"2366","Al-Hasan ibn Ulayl al-Ghazzi narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated: Shayban narrated: from Jabir, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir, he said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, performing Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"2367","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ali ibn Sababah al-Kufi narrated: Amr ibn Akhi al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to me: al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to me: from Jarir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me that I do not withhold anything, I only spend it, he said: O Jarir, there is no blame upon you for withholding your wealth for yourself, for this matter has a limited term."
"2368","Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Mindal ibn Ali narrated: from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Jarir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I only escaped from the polytheists with a slave girl whom I intend for the market, and I practice withdrawal from her. He said: What was decreed for her has come to her."
"2369","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated: from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Jarir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I only escaped from the polytheists with a slave girl, and I practice withdrawal from her, intending her for the market. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What was decreed for her has come to her."
"2370","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated (ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Habib narrated (ha), and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated (ha), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated (ha), and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated; they said: Shuabah narrated: from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, he said: I heard Mundhir ibn Jarir narrating from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the early part of the day when some Bedouin people came, barefoot and naked, wearing striped woolen cloaks slit open, with swords upon them and cloaks. I said: Most of them were from Mudar, indeed all of them were from Mudar. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) change when he saw their condition. He stood and entered, then commanded Bilal, who called the adhan and the iqamah. Then he came out and prayed Zuhr and preached: O mankind, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul, he recited the verse up to His saying: And let every soul look to what it has put forth for tomorrow. Let a man give charity from his dirham, let a man give charity from his dinar, from his sa of dates, from his sa of barley, from such and such, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned even half a date. Then a man came with a bag that his hand could barely carry, or had failed to carry. He said: And the people followed one another until I saw two heaps of food and clothing. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beaming as if it were gilded. He said: Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam, he will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it after him until the Day of Resurrection, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam, upon him will be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it after him until the Day of Resurrection, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2371","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated: Sufyan narrated from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the early part of the day, and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"2372","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) part of the day when some people came, most of them from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar, wearing striped cloaks slit open and girded with swords. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) change when he saw their distress. Then he said: O Bilal, hasten the prayer. When he had prayed, he sat a sitting, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: And fear Allah through whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you. May Allah have mercy on a man who gives charity from his dinar and his dirham and his sa of dates, until he reduced charity to half a date. Among those who stood was a man from the Ansar with a bag that his hand could barely carry, indeed failed to carry, whether it was gold or silver is unknown. Then the people followed one another until they gathered two huge heaps of food and clothing. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beaming as if it were gilded. When the charity ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one of my ummah who institutes a good practice and it is acted upon after him, except that he will have its reward and the like of the reward of those who follow his practice, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, except that upon him will be its burden and the like of the burdens of those who follow his practice, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"2373","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when some people came to him wearing striped cloaks slit open and girded with swords, with no waist-wrappers upon them nor anything else; most of them were from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw their hardship, nakedness, and hunger, his face changed. He entered his house, then went to the mosque and prayed Zuhr, then ascended a small pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, Allah Almighty revealed in His Book: O mankind, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul, to the end of the verse; O you who believe, fear Allah and let every soul look to what it has put forth for tomorrow, up to His saying: They are the successful. Give charity before you cannot give charity. Let a man give charity from his dinar, let a man give charity from his dirham, let a man give charity from his wheat, let a man give charity from his dates, from his barley; do not belittle anything of charity, even half a date. Then a man from the Ansar stood with a bag in his palm and handed it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the pulpit. He took it, and joy was recognized in his face. Then he said: Whoever institutes a good practice and it is acted upon, he will have its reward and the like of the reward of whoever acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice and it is acted upon, upon him will be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it after him, without diminishing anything from their burdens. Then the people stood and dispersed, some with a dinar and some with a dirham, and it was gathered, and he distributed it among them."
"2374","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yahya narrated: from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi: al-Dahhak, the maternal uncle of al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, narrated: from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None shelters a stray animal except one who is astray."
"2375","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated: from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi: al-Dahhak ibn al-Mundhir narrated: from Mundhir ibn Jarir, he said: I was with my father at al-Bawazij when the cattle returned in the evening and he saw a cow he did not recognize. He said to the herdsman: What is this? They said: This is a cow that joined the cattle, unknown whose it is. He ordered that it be driven away until it disappeared from him. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None shelters a stray animal except one who is astray."
"2376","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated (ha), and al-Husayn narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Yala ibn Ubayd narrated; all together from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from al-Dahhak ibn al-Mundhir, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2377","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Sharik informed us (ha), and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Sharik informed us: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no people among whom sins are committed while they are mightier than the sinner and more able to prevent him, and they do not change it, except that Allah strikes them with punishment from it."
"2378","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Mamar informed us: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no people among whom is a man committing sins while they are more able to restrain him and mightier, and they do not change his conduct, except that Allah strikes them with punishment."
"2379","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Shuabah narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people among whom sins are committed while they are mightier and more numerous than the one committing it, and they do not change it, except that Allah strikes them with His punishment."
"2380","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid narrated (ha), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated; both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man among a people committing sins among them, able to change his conduct yet not changing it, except that Allah strikes them with punishment before they die."
"2381","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Sharik narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people among whom is a man committing sins, able to change his conduct yet not changing it, except that Allah envelops them with punishment before they die."
"2382","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated: from Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Jafar al-Farra, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no man dwelling among a people while sins are committed in their midst and they do not restrain him, except that Allah is about to envelop them with punishment from it."
"2383","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated: Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no people among whom is one committing sins while they are more numerous than him and mightier, yet they flatter and remain silent and do not change it, except that punishment befalls them in it."
"2384","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Arafah with his cloak tucked under his arm, raising his hands no higher than his head, while his upper arm muscles trembled."
"2385","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated: Yahya ibn Adam narrated from Ismail, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"2386","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated (ha), and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated: from Zaidah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"2387","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated: my father narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not show mercy to whoever does not show mercy to people."
"2388","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Almighty does not show mercy to whoever does not show mercy to people."
"2389","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated: from al-Hasan al-Bajali, who is Ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ismail ibn Jarir, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts three days of the month, let him fast the white nights: the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth."
"2390","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated (ha), and Fudayl ibn Ahmad al-Malati narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Aban ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated: Ibrahim ibn Jarir narrated: from Jarir, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib sent to me Ibn Abbas and al-Ashath ibn Qays while I was at Qirqisiya, and they said: The Commander of the Faithful conveys greetings to you and says: How excellent is what Allah has shown you in your separation from Muawiyah, and I assign you a rank with me like the rank the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned you. Jarir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen to fight them and to call them to say there is no god but Allah; when they say it, their blood and wealth become inviolable. I will not fight anyone who says there is no god but Allah. So we returned upon that."
"2391","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Aban ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated: Ibrahim ibn Jarir narrated: from his father, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the thicket to relieve himself, then Jarir brought him a small vessel of water, so he cleaned himself, wiped his hand with dust, then washed his face and forearms, wiped over his head and over his leather socks. I said: O Prophet of Allah, your feet? He said: I put them on while they were pure."
"2392","Said ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us: Amr ibn Awn narrated: Hafs ibn Sulayman informed us: from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks, not removing them, then praying in them."
"2393","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated: Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan narrated: Ibrahim ibn Jarir al-Bajali narrated: from his father, he said: Abu Abd Allah went early to al-Kunasah to buy a mount from it, and a freedman of his went early and stood at the side of the market. Mounts began passing by him, and a horse passed by him that pleased him. He said to his freedman: Go and buy that horse. His freedman went and offered its owner three hundred dirhams for it, but its owner refused to sell it, so he haggled with him, but its owner refused to sell it. He said: Will you go to a companion of ours at the side of the market? He said: I do not mind. They both went to him. His freedman said to him: I offered this man three hundred dirhams for his horse but he refused, and he mentioned that it is better than that. The owner of the horse said: He spoke truthfully, may Allah keep you right; do you consider that a price? He said: No, your horse is better than that; will you sell it for five hundred? Until it reached seven hundred dirhams or eight hundred. When the man had gone, he turned to his freedman and said to him: Woe to you, you went to buy a mount for me, a man's mount pleased me, so I sent you to buy it, then you brought a man from among the Muslims leading it while he says: What do you think, what do you think? Yet I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon sincere advice to every Muslim."
"2394","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated: Dawud ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated: Ibrahim ibn Jarir narrated: from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Kill all snakes; whoever spares them fearing their retaliation is not of us."
"2395","Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Asim al-Razi narrated: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated: Dawud al-Awdi narrated: from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats the fourth time, kill him."
"2396","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated: Dawud al-Awdi narrated: from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2397","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated: from Ayyub ibn Jarir, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: Three days for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"2398","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated: Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated: Nasih Abu al-Ala narrated: from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Jarir, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"2399","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Bukayr ibn Amir narrated: from Abu Zurah, he said: Jarir urinated and wiped over the leather socks, and some people objected to him, saying: This was before al-Maidah. He said: I only embraced Islam after al-Maidah was revealed, and I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping except after it was revealed."
"2400","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated (ha), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated; both said: Shuabah narrated: from Ali ibn Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from his grandfather Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me during the Farewell Hajj: Ask the people to be silent. Then he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."
